window.APEX=window.APEX||{};APEX.posts={"order":["knowledge/2-popular-silicone-implant-brands-for-breast-augmentation","knowledge/8-reasons-why-you-should-consider-breast-augmentation-at-apex","knowledge/3-reasons-to-know-before-considering-breast-augmentation","knowledge/2-ways-to-solve-postpartum-sagging-breasts-for-new-mothers","knowledge/11-things-you-should-know-about-breast-augmentation","knowledge/5-factors-to-consider-and-the-benefits-of-choosing-apex-cosmetic-surgery-center","knowledge/3-breast-augmentation-techniques-who-are-they-suitable-for","knowledge/5-advantages-of-minimally-invasive-breast-augmentation-surgery-with-camera-assistance","knowledge/3-techniques-for-beautifully-shaped-chest-enhancement-at-apex","knowledge/corrective-surgery-fix-post-augmentation-issues-for-natural-look","knowledge/4best-techniques-to-lift-and-tighten-the-chest-solving-sagging-problems-effectively","knowledge/two-levels-of-sagging-breasts-and-how-to-firm-them","knowledge/how-to-maintain-beautiful-breasts","knowledge/how-safe-is-cosmetic-surgery-in-thailand","knowledge/essential-tips-for-breast-augmentation-recovery","knowledge/why-is-plastic-surgery-booming-in-thailand","knowledge/essential-insights-for-post-liposuction-recovery","knowledge/understanding-the-recovery-timeline-for-a-breast-lift","knowledge/can-breast-augmentation-be-combined-with-mammogram","knowledge/who-are-the-ideal-candidates-for-liposuction","knowledge/why-do-people-die-from-breast-augmentation","promotion/coolsculpting-fat-reduction-only-8900-thb-from-12500-thb","knowledge/round-vs-teardrop-find-the-best-breast-implant-for-your-body","knowledge/4-chronic-conditions-to-avoid-breast-augmentation","knowledge/how-does-breast-augmentation-differ-for-women-and-lgbt-individuals","knowledge/10-things-to-know-before-considering-breast-augmentation","knowledge/3-reasons-for-stiff-breast-after-breast-augmentation","knowledge/top-5-essential-questions-answered-for-women-considering-breast-surgery","knowledge/what-is-filler-injection","knowledge/how-to-injection-lip-in-older-people","review/breast-augmentation-journey-10-years-of-confidence"],"items":{"knowledge/2-popular-silicone-implant-brands-for-breast-augmentation":{"key":"knowledge/2-popular-silicone-implant-brands-for-breast-augmentation","cat":"Knowledge","title":"2 Popular Silicone Implant Brands for Breast Augmentation","excerpt":"When deciding to undergo breast augmentation, one crucial thing you need to know is the type of silicone breast implants available, their advantages, disadvantages","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/2-popular-silicone-implant-brands-for-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"2 Popular Silicone Implant Brands for Breast Augmentation","h1":"2 Popular Silicone Implant Brands for Breast Augmentation","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/2-popular-silicone-implant-brands-for-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"2 Popular Silicone Implant Brands for Breast Augmentation"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"When deciding to undergo breast augmentation, one crucial thing you need to know is the type of silicone breast implants available, their advantages, disadvantages, and how they will affect the look and feel of your breasts. Additionally, post-augmentation care and precautions are essential to achieve the desired results. Whether it’s post-operative breast massages to prevent implant hardening or selecting the right silicone implant brand, all these factors are critical to consider. In this article, we will explore the differences between two popular silicone implant brands, highlighting their pros and cons."},{"t":"h2","x":"Mentor Silicone Implants"},{"t":"p","x":"Mentor is a highly popular silicone implant brand known for its long-standing reputation and safety. Women trust Mentor implants for their assurance of safety. Additionally, Mentor is a brand manufactured in the United States and certified by the US FDA and the Thai FDA. Mentor implants are available in both textured and smooth surface options. They offer a natural feel with a range of implant shapes, including round and teardrop-shaped implants. This versatility allows for a more personalized outcome, with soft and natural-feeling breasts."},{"t":"h3","x":"Pros:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Mentor implants are known for their cohesive gel, which reduces rippling and provides a more natural appearance."},{"x":"They are available in a variety of shapes, including round and teardrop, catering to individual preferences for a natural look."},{"x":"The softness of Mentor implants enhances their natural feel and touch."}]},{"t":"h3","x":"Cons:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"The cohesive gel makes Mentor implants denser and heavier, which can lead to discomfort or back pain for some individuals."},{"x":"In cases where individuals have very little natural breast tissue, the edges of the implant may be visible."}]},{"t":"h3","x":"Motiva Silicone Implants"},{"t":"p","x":"Motiva is considered one of the premium silicone implant brands available. Motiva implants are known for their Progressive Gel Ultima technology, which provides a soft and natural feel. The texture of Motiva implants is similar to a combination of smooth and textured surfaces, which reduces the risk of implant rippling. These implants are also known for their high elasticity, reducing the chances of capsular contracture (hardening of the breast tissue around the implant)."},{"t":"h3","x":"Pros:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Motiva implants have a faster recovery time and conform well to the body due to their high elasticity."},{"x":"Some Motiva implants have a built-in microchip that stores information about the implant’s model, size, and surgery date, which can be helpful for future reference."},{"x":"Motiva implants come with a leakage warranty for added peace of mind."}]},{"t":"h3","x":"Cons:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Motiva implants tend to be more expensive than other silicone implant brands."},{"x":"The increased elasticity may lead to a slightly longer initial healing period."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Differences in Implant Texture"},{"t":"p","x":"The texture of silicone implants can affect how they feel and behave within the body."},{"t":"h3","x":"Textured Surface:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Textured silicone implants have a slightly rough surface, allowing them to adhere better to the surrounding breast tissue."},{"x":"This texture reduces the risk of implant movement and rotation."}]},{"t":"h3","x":"Smooth Surface:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Smooth silicone implants have a smoother surface, which can move more freely within the breast pocket."},{"x":"They may have a more natural feel and appearance."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Pre-Operative and Post-Operative Considerations"},{"t":"h3","x":"Before undergoing breast augmentation surgery, it’s important to follow certain guidelines:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Avoid food and drink for at least 8 hours before the procedure to reduce the risk of aspiration."},{"x":"Refrain from smoking for at least 2 weeks before surgery, as nicotine can affect blood flow and healing."},{"x":"Avoid alcohol consumption for at least 2 weeks before surgery, as it can impact blood circulation."}]},{"t":"h3","x":"After breast augmentation surgery, follow these post-operative guidelines:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Take prescribed medications as directed by your surgeon to minimize the risk of complications."},{"x":"Avoid smoking and alcohol consumption for an extended period to aid in the healing process."},{"x":"Abstain from vigorous physical activities and exercises that could impact your breast implants for at least 2 months post-surgery."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Regularly attend follow-up appointments with your surgeon to monitor your progress and address any concerns."},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, when considering breast augmentation, it’s crucial to select the right silicone implant brand that suits your needs and preferences. Additionally, proper pre-operative and post-operative care plays a significant role in achieving the best possible results. If you’re seeking a reputable and safe place for breast augmentation, Apex Medical Center is highly recommended, offering experienced surgeons, advanced technology, and excellent patient outcomes."}],"desc":"Discover the advantages of Mentor and Motiva implants at Apex. Choose the best silicone brand for natural feel and safety in breast augmentation today!"},"knowledge/8-reasons-why-you-should-consider-breast-augmentation-at-apex":{"key":"knowledge/8-reasons-why-you-should-consider-breast-augmentation-at-apex","cat":"Knowledge","title":"8 Reasons Why You Should Consider Breast Augmentation at Apex","excerpt":"Breast augmentation is a surgical procedure that requires careful consideration of safety and aesthetics, ensuring natural results after the procedure.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/8-reasons-why-you-should-consider-breast-augmentation-at-apex.webp","alt":"8 Reasons Why You Should Consider Breast Augmentation at Apex","h1":"8 Reasons Why You Should Consider Breast Augmentation at Apex","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/8-reasons-why-you-should-consider-breast-augmentation-at-apex.webp","alt":"8 Reasons Why You Should Consider Breast Augmentation at Apex"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation is a surgical procedure that requires careful consideration of safety and aesthetics, ensuring natural results after the procedure. There are several factors to keep in mind when contemplating breast augmentation, and Apex Medical Center has gathered 8 key reasons to help you make an informed decision. Our center specializes in direct breast augmentation, and we emphasize the expertise of our skilled plastic surgeons, along with the comprehensive care provided by our medical professionals, even after the procedure. Notably, many celebrities have endorsed Apex as the premier destination for breast augmentation. Now, let’s delve into the"},{"t":"h2","x":"8 compelling reasons you should be aware of:"},{"t":"h3","x":"1. Performed by Certified Plastic Surgeons:"},{"t":"p","x":"Before undergoing any cosmetic surgery, it’s essential to assess the credentials and reputation of the plastic surgeon. Apex Medical Center ensures that its surgeons are qualified and certified by medical boards, such as the Medical Council of Thailand, and have completed specialized training in plastic surgery."},{"t":"h3","x":"2. Sterile Operating Rooms at the Highest Safety Level:"},{"t":"p","x":"Apex maintains aseptic conditions in its operating rooms, particularly vital during procedures that involve longer durations. The facility ensures proper temperature control and air circulation within the surgery room, with air turnover rates maintained at 20-25 times per hour. Air filtration systems remove up to 99.99% of impurities, preventing the spread of bacteria."},{"t":"h3","x":"3. Minimally Invasive Techniques Through Endoscopy:"},{"t":"p","x":"The application of endoscopic techniques in breast augmentation enhances surgical precision, yielding superior outcomes. Surgeons use high-resolution cameras to visualize internal structures, providing clarity up to 1,000 times magnification. This approach minimizes blood loss and the risk of complications, while also resulting in smaller incisions and faster recovery."},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Reduced Risk of Nipple Necrosis: Apex surgeons utilize endoscopic methods to accurately identify nerve pathways and blood vessels, reducing the risk of nipple necrosis. By precisely locating these vital structures, the surgery minimizes damage and optimizes blood supply, thereby lowering the chances of nipple-related complications."},{"x":"Smaller Incisions and Faster Recovery: Endoscopic techniques result in smaller incisions compared to traditional methods, as the camera provides a detailed view of tissues. The reduction in trauma leads to a quicker recovery period, enabling patients to return to their daily routines sooner and with greater comfort."}]},{"t":"h3","x":"4. Expert Anesthesia Monitoring for Optimal Safety:"},{"t":"p","x":"Procedures involving longer surgical durations require careful anesthesia management. Apex ensures vigilant oversight by specialized anesthesiologists throughout the surgery. They closely monitor vital signs and administer anesthesia to maintain patient safety and comfort."},{"t":"h3","x":"5. Comprehensive VIP Care During Recovery:"},{"t":"p","x":"Apex Medical Center offers a VIP recovery experience to ensure a comfortable and safe recuperation period. Patients are accommodated in well-appointed rooms, featuring panoramic views of Bangkok. Round-the-clock nursing care is provided to cater to every need, ensuring a worry-free and relaxing recovery."},{"t":"h3","x":"6. Celebrity Endorsements:"},{"t":"p","x":"Numerous celebrities have endorsed Apex as the ultimate destination for breast augmentation. Renowned personalities, such as Dr. Somboon Waiprib, have confirmed the exceptional quality of care and results delivered by Apex Medical Center."},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, breast augmentation at Apex Medical Center stands out for its commitment to safety, expertise of skilled surgeons, cutting-edge technology, and comprehensive post-operative care. These 8 compelling reasons highlight the unparalleled advantages of choosing Apex for your breast augmentation journey. Your decision should be well-informed, and Apex Medical Center ensures that your experience is safe, comfortable, and exceptional in every aspect."},{"t":"p","x":"Celebrity Clients Who Have Received Breast Enhancement Services at APEX"},{"t":"p","x":"Renowned celebrities who have sought breast enhancement services at APEX Medical Center have openly praised the natural, beautiful, and confident results they achieved. It’s no wonder why they chose to entrust APEX with their breast enhancement needs. Let’s delve into the reasons behind their confidence and trust in APEX’s care."},{"t":"p","x":"Thank You: Already a fan of bikinis and swimwear, Thank You desired an even more appealing and sexy bust. Her decision to trust APEX was solidified by the numerous positive reviews she encountered. Thank You’s concern was asymmetry, with one breast slightly smaller than the other. However, APEX’s skilled doctors provided personalized techniques to ensure symmetry and eliminate her worries."},{"t":"p","x":"Toktak: Seeking breast enhancement, Toktak consulted with Dr. Somboon Waiprib at APEX. Toktak emphasized that she did not face major concerns before the procedure, except for a potential issue of back pain that developed approximately 10 years after her initial breast augmentation. Toktak acknowledges that techniques for breast enhancement have evolved since her first procedure, leading to a slightly elevated appearance. Dr. Somboon Waiprib’s guidance ensured the right approach, size, and proportions, resulting in natural-looking results."},{"t":"p","x":"Kluay: Kluay’s journey with APEX involved addressing various concerns before undergoing breast enhancement. As a performer, she aimed to exude confidence and elegance on stage, which necessitated a boost in self-assurance through breast enhancement. However, Kluay tackled the issue from various angles, even resorting to tightly wrapping her chest with tape, making singing challenging. After seeking advice from Dr. Somboon Waiprib, Kluay received detailed recommendations for the procedure’s specifics, including size and proportions, allowing her to achieve a harmonious and natural appearance while maintaining her vocal abilities."},{"t":"h3","x":"7. Highly Acclaimed Awards:"},{"t":"p","x":"APEX, a comprehensive beauty center with expertise in aesthetics and led by experienced specialists, has earned prestigious accolades. Dr. Somboon Waiprib, a renowned plastic surgeon, has been recognized with the Global Health Asia Pacific award for three consecutive years and the Motiva Joy Partner award for two consecutive years. These awards reaffirm APEX’s leadership in innovative beauty treatments. Dr. Somboon Waiprib, the sole Thai physician to present surgical outcomes internationally at conferences such as IMCAS, continues to pioneer comprehensive beauty solutions."},{"t":"h3","x":"8. Postoperative Care Excellence:"},{"t":"p","x":"A crucial aspect of APEX’s care is its unparalleled postoperative support, crucial for the recovery phase after breast enhancement. Recognizing the initial concerns and anxieties following surgery, APEX provides dedicated nursing care and post-surgical consultations. Additionally, APEX offers 100% pure oxygen Hyperbaric Oxygen therapy, promoting rapid healing, reducing discomfort and swelling, and enhancing overall well-being."},{"t":"p","x":"For those researching top destinations for breast enhancement, APEX Medical Center stands out as a premier choice. With the eight compelling reasons mentioned above, APEX prioritizes patient safety and guarantees highly effective, natural-looking results."}],"desc":"Discover 8 reasons why Apex is the ideal choice for breast augmentation. Expert care and exceptional results."},"knowledge/3-reasons-to-know-before-considering-breast-augmentation":{"key":"knowledge/3-reasons-to-know-before-considering-breast-augmentation","cat":"Knowledge","title":"3 Reasons to Know Before Considering Breast Augmentation","excerpt":"Breast augmentation has become quite common in today’s era of beauty enhancement, with advancements in technology and innovations ensuring safe and effective procedures.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/3-reasons-to-know-before-considering-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"3 Reasons to Know Before Considering Breast Augmentation","h1":"3 Reasons to Know Before Considering Breast Augmentation","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/3-reasons-to-know-before-considering-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"3 Reasons to Know Before Considering Breast Augmentation"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation has become quite common in today’s era of beauty enhancement, with advancements in technology and innovations ensuring safe and effective procedures. In this regard, we wish to share and provide valuable insights to all the women seeking information about breast augmentation. Here, we present three crucial factors to consider before opting for a safe and risk-free breast augmentation experience."},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Make an Informed Decision Breast augmentation involves surgical procedures that come with risks and potential impacts on your body. Therefore, when contemplating breast augmentation, it’s essential to carefully consider your reasons for wanting the procedure and the desired outcomes. For example, some might think that bigger is always better when it comes to breast size. However, it’s important to recognize that excessively large breast implants can lead to health issues such as back and neck pain, and even implant displacement due to excessive strain on the body’s natural structure. So, before you decide to enhance your breast size, think deeply about these consequences."},{"x":"Ensure Trustworthy Silicone Implants Whether you’re considering textured or smooth silicone breast implants, they must meet the standards set by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) and be properly certified. To illustrate, imagine someone like “A” who initially consulted a doctor about using a particular brand and size of silicone implants. However, during the actual surgery, a different brand was used without “A’s” knowledge. After the surgery, complications arose, indicating potential leakage or rupture. This emphasizes the significance of verifying the authenticity of the implants being used through thorough research on the surgeon’s background, hospital or clinic history, and other related factors."},{"x":"Choose Trustworthy Surgeons and Centers The foremost consideration before undergoing any surgical procedure is selecting a qualified and accredited surgeon. A certified surgeon should have credentials from the Medical Council of Thailand and the Medical Board, signifying their expertise and specialized training in cosmetic surgery. Dr. Somboon Waiprib, for example, stands as a distinguished surgeon who has received accolades like the Global Health Asia Pacific award three years in a row. This assures individuals seeking breast augmentation that Apex Medical Center delivers guaranteed safety and exceptional results."}]},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, Apex Medical Center stands as a reputable beauty enhancement center that employs meticulous procedures to treat patients’ concerns directly, under the supervision of specialized medical practitioners. Therefore, individuals can confidently trust that breast augmentation procedures at Apex will not only yield favorable results but also guarantee safety and minimal impact on their daily lives."}],"desc":"Consider these 3 important factors before breast augmentation. Apex provides expert guidance to ensure the best results."},"knowledge/2-ways-to-solve-postpartum-sagging-breasts-for-new-mothers":{"key":"knowledge/2-ways-to-solve-postpartum-sagging-breasts-for-new-mothers","cat":"Knowledge","title":"2 Ways to Solve Postpartum Sagging Breasts for New Mothers","excerpt":"One of the common challenges that new mothers often face after childbirth is the issue of sagging and loose breasts.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/2-ways-to-solve-postpartum-sagging-breasts-for-new-mothers.webp","alt":"2 Ways to Solve Postpartum Sagging Breasts for New Mothers","h1":"2 Ways to Solve Postpartum Sagging Breasts for New Mothers","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/2-ways-to-solve-postpartum-sagging-breasts-for-new-mothers.webp","alt":"2 Ways to Solve Postpartum Sagging Breasts for New Mothers"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"One of the common challenges that new mothers often face after childbirth is the issue of sagging and loose breasts. During breastfeeding, breasts tend to increase in size, but over time, as breastfeeding pauses, breasts may shrink in size and begin to show signs of sagging. However, it’s important to note that sagging breasts can occur for women of all ages, not just postpartum mothers. These changes often lead to feelings of insecurity and continuous discomfort for many women."},{"t":"h2","x":"1. Breast Lift Surgery"},{"t":"p","x":"Breast lift surgery is a common solution for addressing sagging breasts. This surgical procedure involves removing excess skin and fat tissue from beneath the breast area. The surgeon will lift and reshape the breasts, ensuring both sides are balanced and at an even level. It’s important to choose an experienced surgeon for this procedure, as the breast area contains many nerves, and improper surgery could lead to complications such as numbness. Recovery after breast lift surgery usually takes around 1-2 weeks for the breasts to settle into their new position. However, it’s essential to select a reputable medical facility and skilled surgeon to avoid potential long-term complications."},{"t":"h3","x":"Breast Lift Techniques"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Donut Technique: Suitable for mild to moderate sagging. The surgeon makes a circular incision around the areola (nipple area) and tightens the skin by suturing it around the areola."},{"x":"Crescent Technique: Suitable for slight sagging. This technique involves making an incision along the upper half of the areola and lifting the breast tissue slightly. It takes around 2-3 hours and results in a minor lift."},{"x":"Lollipop Technique: Suitable for moderate sagging. This method involves an incision around the areola and a vertical incision down the breast, creating a lollipop-like shape. Excess skin and tissue are removed, and the breast is lifted and reshaped."},{"x":"Anchor Technique: Suitable for severe sagging. This technique involves incisions around the areola, vertically down the breast, and horizontally along the breast crease. It’s suitable for significant sagging and provides a comprehensive lift and reshaping."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"2. Breast Augmentation for Tightening"},{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation, or breast implants, can also help tighten and lift sagging breasts. If your breasts have lost volume and firmness, implants can restore their fullness and improve their shape. This procedure involves inserting silicone or saline implants either under or over the chest muscles. It’s essential to discuss your preferences and desired outcome with your surgeon to achieve the best results."},{"t":"p","x":"It’s important to note that individual experiences and solutions may vary. Consulting with a qualified medical professional is crucial to determine the most suitable approach for your unique situation. At Apex Medical Center, we focus on providing personalized beauty care and boosting self-confidence. Our experts can assess and analyze your needs to provide the best solution for you, whether it’s breast lift surgery or breast augmentation."}],"desc":"Address postpartum sagging with Apex's expert solutions. Discover breast lift and augmentation options for renewed confidence and a rejuvenated appearance."},"knowledge/11-things-you-should-know-about-breast-augmentation":{"key":"knowledge/11-things-you-should-know-about-breast-augmentation","cat":"Knowledge","title":"11 things you should know about breast augmentation","excerpt":"Breast augmentation is a surgical procedure aimed at enhancing the size and shape of the breasts. It is a popular cosmetic surgery option chosen by many individuals seeking to improve their self-confidence and body image.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/11-things-you-should-know-about-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"11 things you should know about breast augmentation","h1":"11 things you should know about breast augmentation","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/11-things-you-should-know-about-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"11 things you should know about breast augmentation"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation is a surgical procedure aimed at enhancing the size and shape of the breasts. It is a popular cosmetic surgery option chosen by many individuals seeking to improve their self-confidence and body image. In this comprehensive article, we will address the most commonly asked questions about breast augmentation and provide detailed answers to each one. Additionally, we will discuss the factors that people consider when deciding on breast augmentation. Lastly, we will highlight Apex Medical Center, a renowned facility led by board-certified plastic surgeons, which has been awarded the prestigious Apex Award for Best Cosmetic Surgery by Asia Pacific Health for three consecutive years."},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"What is breast augmentation? Breast augmentation is a surgical procedure that involves the placement of breast implants to increase the size and improve the shape of the breasts. It is typically performed under general anesthesia and can be tailored to the individual’s desired outcome."},{"x":"How is breast augmentation surgery performed? Breast augmentation surgery typically involves the following steps: pre-operative consultation, anesthesia administration, incision placement, creation of a pocket, insertion of implants, and closure of incisions. The choice of incision location and implant placement depends on various factors, including the individual’s anatomy and preferences."},{"x":"What are the different types of breast implants? The two primary types of breast implants used in augmentation surgery are saline and silicone implants. Saline implants are filled with sterile saltwater, while silicone implants are filled with a cohesive silicone gel. Both types have advantages and considerations that should be discussed with a board-certified plastic surgeon."},{"x":"How long does breast augmentation surgery take? The duration of breast augmentation surgery varies depending on several factors, including the complexity of the procedure, the surgeon’s experience, and the individual’s unique circumstances. On average, the surgery can last between one to three hours."},{"x":"What is the recovery time after breast augmentation? Recovery after breast augmentation is a gradual process. Most individuals can expect some discomfort, swelling, and bruising in the days following surgery. It is important to follow post-operative instructions provided by the surgeon, which may include wearing a surgical bra, avoiding strenuous activities, and attending follow-up appointments."},{"x":"What are the risks and complications associated with breast augmentation? As with any surgical procedure, breast augmentation carries some risks. These may include infection, bleeding, adverse reaction to anesthesia, implant rupture, capsular contracture, changes in nipple sensation, and dissatisfaction with the aesthetic outcome. However, serious complications are rare, especially when the surgery is performed by a qualified plastic surgeon."},{"x":"Can breast implants affect breastfeeding? Breast implants do not necessarily preclude an individual from breastfeeding. In most cases, breast augmentation does not interfere with the ability to breastfeed. However, it is important to discuss any plans for future breastfeeding with your surgeon during the consultation."},{"x":"Will breast augmentation leave visible scars? Like any surgical procedure, breast augmentation will leave some degree of scarring. However, the extent and visibility of scars can be minimized through careful incision placement and post-operative scar management techniques. The surgeon will discuss the various incision options and their potential scarring outcomes during the consultation."},{"x":"How much does breast augmentation cost? The cost of breast augmentation varies depending on several factors, including the surgeon’s experience, geographical location, facility fees, anesthesia fees, and the type of implants used. It is important to obtain a comprehensive cost estimate during the initial consultation, which may include all associated expenses."},{"x":"How long do breast implants last? Breast implants are not considered lifetime devices and may require replacement or removal at some point in the future. The lifespan of implants varies, but many manufacturers provide warranties for a specified period, typically around 10 to 15 years."},{"x":"Can breast implants rupture or leak? Breast implants can potentially rupture or leak over time. The risk of rupture is higher in saline implants compared to silicone implants. If a rupture occurs, the implant may need to be removed or replaced. Regular monitoring and follow-up visits with a plastic surgeon are important to ensure the continued integrity of the implants."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Conclusion: Breast augmentation is a popular cosmetic surgery procedure that can enhance the size and shape of the breasts, helping individuals achieve their desired aesthetic goals. By addressing the most commonly asked questions regarding breast augmentation and highlighting the factors people consider when making their decision, individuals can make informed choices and have realistic expectations. Apex Medical Center, led by board-certified plastic surgeons, has received the prestigious Apex Award for Best Cosmetic Surgery by Asia Pacific Health for three consecutive years, attesting to their expertise and commitment to providing exceptional care in the field of cosmetic surgery. If you are considering breast augmentation, consult with a qualified plastic surgeon to discuss your specific goals and determine the best approach for you."}],"desc":"Experience advanced breast augmentation with camera-assisted techniques. Enjoy precise results, minimal scarring, and faster recovery for optimal outcomes."},"knowledge/5-factors-to-consider-and-the-benefits-of-choosing-apex-cosmetic-surgery-center":{"key":"knowledge/5-factors-to-consider-and-the-benefits-of-choosing-apex-cosmetic-surgery-center","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Choose Apex: Expert Care & Benefits for Your Cosmetic Surgery","excerpt":"Breast augmentation is a popular cosmetic procedure that allows individuals to enhance the size and shape of their breasts. When considering breast augmentation","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/5-factors-to-consider-and-the-benefits-of-choosing.webp","alt":"Expert Care & Benefits for Your Cosmetic Surgery","h1":"Choose Apex: Expert Care & Benefits for Your Cosmetic Surgery","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/5-factors-to-consider-and-the-benefits-of-choosing.webp","alt":"Expert Care & Benefits for Your Cosmetic Surgery"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation is a popular cosmetic procedure that allows individuals to enhance the size and shape of their breasts. When considering breast augmentation, there are several factors that individuals prioritize to ensure a safe and effective outcome. In this article, we will explore the most common factors that people consider when making their decision and highlight the benefits of choosing Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center in Bangkok and Phuket for breast augmentation. Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center is renowned for its qualified plastic surgeons, experienced anesthesiologists, state-of-the-art operating theaters, and advanced breast augmentation-assisted machines. Let’s delve into the factors individuals consider and why Apex is an excellent choice for breast augmentation."},{"t":"h2","x":"Factors to Consider when Choosing Breast Augmentation :"},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Surgeon’s Qualification and Experience: One of the primary factors to consider when choosing breast augmentation is the qualification and experience of the plastic surgeon. Patients should seek a board-certified plastic surgeon with expertise in breast augmentation procedures. Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center boasts a team of highly qualified and experienced plastic surgeons who have a track record of successful breast augmentation surgeries."},{"x":"Anesthesiologist’s Expertise: The role of an anesthesiologist in breast augmentation surgery is crucial for patient safety and comfort. Apex ensures that their team includes qualified anesthesiologists who specialize in cosmetic surgery procedures. This ensures that patients receive the highest standard of anesthesia care throughout the surgery."},{"x":"Operating Theater Standards: The quality and safety of the operating theater are paramount in any surgical procedure. Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center is equipped with state-of-the-art operating theaters that adhere to strict hygiene and safety protocols. Their 10K operating theaters provide a sterile environment, reducing the risk of infections and complications."},{"x":"Breast Augmentation-Assisted Machines: Advanced breast augmentation-assisted machines contribute to better surgical outcomes and patient satisfaction. Apex is at the forefront of technology, offering the latest and most effective breast augmentation-assisted machines. These machines aid in precise implant placement, resulting in natural-looking and symmetrical breasts."},{"x":"Safety Protocols and Patient Care: Patient safety should always be a priority. Apex ensures that comprehensive safety protocols are in place to minimize risks and complications associated with breast augmentation surgery. Additionally, their dedicated and compassionate staff provide personalized care and support throughout the entire treatment journey."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Benefits of Choosing Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center"},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Excellence in Plastic Surgery: Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center has established itself as a leader in the field of plastic surgery. With a team of highly qualified plastic surgeons who stay updated with the latest techniques and advancements, patients can expect exceptional results. The center’s reputation for excellence attracts patients from around the world seeking top-notch breast augmentation procedures."},{"x":"Patient-Centric Approach: At Apex, patient satisfaction and well-being are at the core of their practice. They take the time to understand each patient’s unique goals and expectations, tailoring the breast augmentation procedure to meet their specific needs. The center’s patient-centric approach ensures a personalized experience and helps achieve optimal results."},{"x":"Comprehensive Consultation Process: Before any surgical procedure, Apex conducts thorough consultations to educate patients about the breast augmentation process, discuss options, and address any concerns. The surgeons provide detailed information on implant types, sizes, incision techniques, and expected outcomes. This comprehensive approach empowers patients to make informed decisions."},{"x":"Emphasis on Natural Results: Natural-looking results are a key priority at Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center. The skilled surgeons work closely with patients to achieve harmonious and proportionate breast enhancement. Through meticulous planning and precise surgical techniques, Apex ensures that the results complement the patient’s overall physique, resulting in aesthetically pleasing and natural-looking breasts."},{"x":"Postoperative Care and Follow-up: Apex is committed to providing comprehensive postoperative care and follow-up to ensure the best possible recovery for patients. Their dedicated team provides detailed aftercare instructions, regular check-ups, and ongoing support during the healing process. This commitment to postoperative care enhances patient satisfaction and contributes to successful outcomes."},{"x":"Apex’s Prestigious Accolades: Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center has received the prestigious Apex Award for Best Cosmetic Surgery by Asia Pacific Health for three consecutive years. This recognition speaks to the center’s commitment to excellence, patient safety, and exceptional results. Patients can have confidence in choosing Apex for their breast augmentation procedure."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Choosing the right cosmetic surgery center is crucial when considering breast augmentation. Apex Cosmetic Surgery Center in Bangkok and Phuket offers a compelling choice with its qualified plastic surgeons, experienced anesthesiologists, state-of-the-art operating theaters, and advanced breast augmentation-assisted machines. By prioritizing factors such as surgeon qualification, safety protocols, and patient-centered care, Apex ensures the maximum effectiveness and safety of the breast augmentation procedure. Additionally, the center’s accolades, including the Apex Award for Best Cosmetic Surgery, validate its excellence in the field. Patients can trust Apex to provide personalized care, natural-looking results, and a seamless journey throughout their breast augmentation experience."}],"desc":"Breast augmentation is a popular cosmetic procedure that allows individuals to enhance the size and shape of their breasts."},"knowledge/3-breast-augmentation-techniques-who-are-they-suitable-for":{"key":"knowledge/3-breast-augmentation-techniques-who-are-they-suitable-for","cat":"Knowledge","title":"3 “Breast Augmentation” Techniques, Who Are They Suitable For?","excerpt":"Breast augmentation is a popular surgical procedure that many women opt for to enhance their body shape and boost their confidence.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/3-breast-augmentation-techniques-who-are-they-suitable-for.webp","alt":"3 “Breast Augmentation” Techniques, Who Are They Suitable For?","h1":"3 “Breast Augmentation” Techniques, Who Are They Suitable For?","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/3-breast-augmentation-techniques-who-are-they-suitable-for.webp","alt":"3 “Breast Augmentation” Techniques, Who Are They Suitable For?"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation is a popular surgical procedure that many women opt for to enhance their body shape and boost their confidence. Choosing to undergo breast augmentation is an important decision that requires careful consideration, as it can have an impact on both the body and overall health, both before and after the procedure. Therefore, selecting a reputable and high-quality facility is crucial."},{"t":"p","x":"If you are looking for a reliable place to have breast augmentation, Apex Medical Center is a well-known establishment that specializes in breast augmentation surgeries in Thailand. They have a team of skilled and experienced medical professionals who are experts in the field of breast augmentation, including both silicone-based and fat grafting procedures."},{"t":"p","x":"Apex Medical Center maintains high standards in providing comprehensive care from the initial consultation to post-operative care. They utilize modern technology to ensure beautiful and proportionate results. Moreover, they employ advanced medical instruments and equipment to ensure accurate outcomes."},{"t":"h2","x":"Current Breast Augmentation Techniques:"},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Silicone Implants: This is the most common technique used in breast augmentation. Silicone implants involve placing silicone gel-filled implants behind the breast tissue to increase the size and shape of the breasts. The procedure is performed through a small incision, and the silicone implants are inserted through the opening. Silicone implants allow for customized size and shape to meet the patient’s desired outcome."},{"x":"Fat Grafting: This technique involves harvesting fat from other areas of the body, such as the hips or arms, and injecting it into the breasts to enhance and improve their shape. Fat grafting is considered more natural as it utilizes the patient’s own fat, and it can result in well-proportioned and aesthetically pleasing breast augmentation."},{"x":"Combination Technique: Sometimes, a combination of silicone implants and fat grafting may be used to achieve the most desirable and beautiful results."}]},{"t":"p","x":"The appropriate breast augmentation technique for you will depend on your body’s characteristics and personal preferences. Therefore, it is recommended to consult with a qualified surgeon or plastic surgeon to discuss the suitable technique and gather more information. Checking the medical professional’s credentials, experience, and track record is essential when selecting a facility for your breast augmentation procedure."},{"t":"p","x":"In summary, Apex Medical Center is a reputable and high-quality establishment for breast augmentation procedures. They have a team of experienced and attentive medical professionals who prioritize patient care. If you are seeking a trustworthy and quality facility for breast augmentation, Apex Medical Center, recipient of the prestigious Global Health Asia Pacific Award for three consecutive years and the JOY by Motiva Award for two consecutive years, can be considered as a reliable choice."}],"desc":"Discover three breast augmentation techniques at Apex. Find the right solution based on your body type and goals."},"knowledge/5-advantages-of-minimally-invasive-breast-augmentation-surgery-with-camera-assistance":{"key":"knowledge/5-advantages-of-minimally-invasive-breast-augmentation-surgery-with-camera-assistance","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Advanced Breast Augmentation: Precision with Camera Assistance","excerpt":"Innovations in the field of breast augmentation surgery through camera-assisted techniques have significantly improved the efficiency and effectiveness of surgical outcomes.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/5-advantages-of-minimally-invasive-breast-augmentation-en.webp","alt":"Advanced Breast Augmentation: Precision with Camera Assistance","h1":"Advanced Breast Augmentation: Precision with Camera Assistance","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/5-advantages-of-minimally-invasive-breast-augmentation-en.webp","alt":"Advanced Breast Augmentation: Precision with Camera Assistance"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Innovations in the field of breast augmentation surgery through camera-assisted techniques have significantly improved the efficiency and effectiveness of surgical outcomes. Primarily developed by expert surgical teams, this technique aims to provide clear visualization of internal tissue structures and precise details, magnified up to 1,000 times. Additionally, camera-assisted surgery offers several advantages over traditional methods, encompassing five key benefits. Let’s explore these advantages:"},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"High Precision Camera-assisted surgeries utilize high-resolution cameras, allowing surgeons to display internal structures with remarkable clarity and precision, surpassing the capabilities of traditional techniques."},{"x":"Reduced Blood Loss Apart from offering clear visualization, camera-assisted surgery minimizes blood loss during the procedure. The camera’s ability to identify blood vessels and other intricate details that are not visible to the naked eye contributes to this reduced blood loss."},{"x":"Mitigated Risk of Nipple Necrosis An inherent risk in breast augmentation surgery is the possibility of nipple necrosis due to the dense network of nerves in the breast area. Camera-assisted surgery aids in precise identification of nerve locations, significantly reducing the risk of nipple necrosis."},{"x":"Minimal Incision Scarring The effectiveness of camera-assisted breast augmentation lies in the surgeon’s ability to assess tissue abnormalities through the camera, resulting in smaller incisions. Unlike wide incisions in traditional methods, these smaller incisions translate to minimal scarring once the surgical site has healed."},{"x":"Faster Recovery Due to the minimal tissue disruption and trauma associated with camera-assisted surgery, patients tend to experience faster recovery times compared to conventional procedures. This results in a quicker return to normal activities."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Performing breast augmentation surgery using camera-assisted techniques requires a specialized team of expert surgeons in the field. Without such expertise, there’s a risk of severe complications. At Apex Medical Center, our team comprises highly skilled surgeons specializing in camera-assisted breast augmentation. Led by a professor-level surgeon who was honored with the Global Health Asia Pacific 2019 award for excellence in surgical practice, our team possesses over 15 years of experience. This assures patients that opting for breast augmentation surgery at our center guarantees both safety and significantly improved outcomes."}],"desc":"Get informed with Apex's guide on breast augmentation. Discover essential insights for enhancing your confidence and body image with expert care."},"knowledge/3-techniques-for-beautifully-shaped-chest-enhancement-at-apex":{"key":"knowledge/3-techniques-for-beautifully-shaped-chest-enhancement-at-apex","cat":"Knowledge","title":"3 Techniques for Beautifully Shaped Chest Enhancement at APEX","excerpt":"Chest enhancement is a surgical procedure that requires specific techniques and the expertise of a confident surgeon who specializes in breast augmentation.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/3-techniques-for-beautifully-shaped-chest-enhancement-en.webp","alt":"3 Techniques for Beautifully Shaped Chest Enhancement at APEX","h1":"3 Techniques for Beautifully Shaped Chest Enhancement at APEX","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/3-techniques-for-beautifully-shaped-chest-enhancement-en.webp","alt":"3 Techniques for Beautifully Shaped Chest Enhancement at APEX"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Chest enhancement is a surgical procedure that requires specific techniques and the expertise of a confident surgeon who specializes in breast augmentation. Additionally, various factors play a crucial role in achieving the best possible results from chest enhancement. One of the main concerns for individuals undergoing chest enhancement is the appearance of scars, as scars can be a source of unnatural feelings. Some people who have undergone chest enhancement may have large scars or uneven scar tissue. Today, we will address the factors that contribute to large scars in chest enhancement."},{"t":"h2","x":"Surgeons with Expertise and Excellent Chest Enhancement Techniques"},{"t":"p","x":"First and foremost, before undergoing surgery, it is essential to ensure that the surgeon is highly skilled and holds the appropriate qualifications and specialist certifications. These qualifications are obtained from medical institutions such as the Royal College of Surgeons of Thailand and the Medical Council, as part of specialized training in the field of plastic and reconstructive surgery. These programs typically span either 5 or 7 years, as in the case of Dr. Somboon Waiprib, who has a complete and comprehensive profile as mentioned above. Additionally, Dr. Somboon Waiprib has been awarded the Global Health Asia Pacific Award for three consecutive years, providing those seeking information about chest enhancement with confidence in the quality and safety of the procedure at APEX."},{"t":"h2","x":"Camera-Assisted Chest Enhancement for Smaller Scars"},{"t":"p","x":"For those concerned about the appearance of scars after chest enhancement surgery, these concerns can be alleviated. APEX Medical Center employs cutting-edge camera-assisted surgical techniques, which are highly advanced for modern times. Camera-assisted chest enhancement surgery enhances the precision and accuracy of the procedure by providing clear, detailed views of internal structures. Naturally, not everything can be seen with the naked eye, making camera-assisted chest enhancement a crucial advancement. This method minimizes bleeding during surgery, reduces scar size, and accelerates the recovery process compared to traditional surgical techniques."},{"t":"h2","x":"Chest Enhancement Using Implants"},{"t":"p","x":"Another technique that APEX Medical Center finds suitable for individuals seeking chest enhancement is the use of “implants with cups.” This technique reduces scar size significantly. The advantages of using implants made of polyfiber film material include their transparency and flexibility. Additionally, they are coated with a special substance for maximum patient benefit. This technique also reduces friction between the silicone and other tissues in the body."},{"t":"p","x":"Clearly, chest enhancement is a major surgical procedure, and the experience of the surgeon directly affects the results. APEX Medical Center is another beauty enhancement institution that offers chest enhancement with the utmost patient safety. The surgical process and steps are performed under the care of highly experienced surgeons, specifically at the professor level, with over 20 years of experience, and recognized as the top beauty surgeons, including being awarded the Global Health Asia Pacific Award. Advanced technology and tools are used, including a sterile 10K operating room (suitable for heart and brain surgeries) and a VIP recovery room with 24-hour nursing care. Silicone implants are guaranteed for life, and during the surgical period, patients are closely monitored and administered medications under the supervision of specialist physicians. With this assurance, chest enhancement at APEX is undoubtedly a path to achieving guaranteed and excellent results."}],"desc":"Enhance your chest with Apex's advanced techniques. Achieve beautifully shaped results with expert care and precision for a confident, stunning silhouette."},"knowledge/corrective-surgery-fix-post-augmentation-issues-for-natural-look":{"key":"knowledge/corrective-surgery-fix-post-augmentation-issues-for-natural-look","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Corrective Surgery: Fix Post-Augmentation Issues for Natural Look","excerpt":"The issue faced by women who have undergone breast augmentation – why would they need to fix their breasts? Today, Apex has the answer.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/4-problems-faced-by-women-who.webp","alt":"Fix Post-Augmentation Issues for Natural Look","h1":"Corrective Surgery: Fix Post-Augmentation Issues for Natural Look","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/4-problems-faced-by-women-who.webp","alt":"Fix Post-Augmentation Issues for Natural Look"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The issue faced by women who have undergone breast augmentation – why would they need to fix their breasts? Today, Apex has the answer. If we rewind back to the past, the prevailing trend for breast augmentation was to go big initially to avoid regret later. However, due to the changing times that have brought about shifts in breast augmentation trends, 2023 has witnessed adaptations. That adaptation is achieving breast augmentation that aligns with proportion or getting breast augmentation that perfectly fits one’s body."},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"The Problem with Breast Augmentation: Correcting Breast Proportions Breasts that have previously been augmented tend to be excessively large. As I mentioned earlier, the changing times have led to shifts in breast augmentation trends. That shift is towards achieving breast augmentation that aligns with proportion, resulting in more natural-looking breasts. This approach ensures that the breasts appear natural in various outfits and reduces the likelihood of sagging around silicone implants. It also decreases the risk of stretch marks and visible silicone implant ripples."},{"x":"Health Problems Arising from Overly Large Breasts Breast augmentation resulting in excessively large breasts can lead to health issues such as back and neck pain. This is because larger silicone implants, due to their weight, can strain the body. Some individuals might struggle to carry this added weight, eventually leading to health problems as mentioned earlier."},{"x":"Breast Spacing, Height, and Proximity Issues Well-done breast augmentation should consider natural proportions to create a natural appearance. In the past, surgical techniques might not have been as refined as they are today. This could result in augmented breasts that appeared too spaced apart, too high, or too close together. Such cases were often colloquially referred to as “twin peaks.”"},{"x":"Complications like Implant Rupture or Capsular Contracture Complications like implant rupture or the tightening of scar tissue around implants can alter the shape of augmented breasts over time. This is due to the body’s response to silicone implants. Sometimes, the scar tissue formation is minimal, but in some cases, it can lead to an unnatural breast appearance and even pain around the breast area."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Advantages of Proportional Breast Augmentation"},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Helps reduce the occurrence of implant rippling around silicone implants. When breasts are augmented to an excessively large size, the subsequent effects can cause the silicone implant to ripple and create an uneven texture."},{"x":"Reduces excessive breast sagging that appears more than usual. The increased weight of larger silicone implants can lead to excessive breast sagging, which can be alleviated by achieving a proportional breast size. This not only eliminates concerns about this issue but also better aligns with the individual’s body proportions."},{"x":"Decreases the risk of visible stretch marks and implant ripples. From an external perspective, having naturally-feeling breasts with soft texture enhances overall body symmetry. According to inquiries made to Apex Medical Center, some individuals mentioned that people around them didn’t even realize they had undergone breast augmentation."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Why Choose Apex for Breast Augmentation Apex Medical Center is a comprehensive beauty center equipped with state-of-the-art technology and medical instruments. The operating rooms meet the highest safety standards, equivalent to those found in large hospitals. The skilled surgical teams, led by proficient surgeons, perform breast augmentation surgeries directly. The head surgeon is an award-winning expert, receiving the highest accolade in surgical excellence from Global Health Asia Pacific for three consecutive years. With over 15 years of extensive experience, patients can trust that their breast augmentation procedures at Apex Medical Center will yield safe and definite improvements."}],"desc":"Learn about the 4 common issues women face after breast augmentation. Apex offers solutions to fix and enhance results for lasting satisfaction."},"knowledge/4best-techniques-to-lift-and-tighten-the-chest-solving-sagging-problems-effectively":{"key":"knowledge/4best-techniques-to-lift-and-tighten-the-chest-solving-sagging-problems-effectively","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Lift & Tighten: Effective Techniques to Solve Chest Sagging","excerpt":"The chest is an essential part that empowers confidence when wearing beautiful clothes for women like us. When the components of the chest harmonize with the body’s proportions","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/effective-techniques-to-solve-chest-sagging.webp","alt":"Effective Techniques to Solve Chest Sagging","h1":"Lift & Tighten: Effective Techniques to Solve Chest Sagging","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/effective-techniques-to-solve-chest-sagging.webp","alt":"Effective Techniques to Solve Chest Sagging"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"The chest is an essential part that empowers confidence when wearing beautiful clothes for women like us. When the components of the chest harmonize with the body’s proportions, it greatly enhances a woman’s pride in her chest. However, beyond this, there are many women who hesitate to reveal their less firm chest. These issues can lead to a loss of self-confidence. Several factors contribute to chest sagging, such as:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Pregnancy and Breastfeeding: Hormonal changes during pregnancy and breastfeeding can cause the breasts to enlarge. After this phase, hormone production ceases, and the breasts may become smaller and less firm."},{"x":"Improper Weight Loss: Rapid weight loss affects the breast area as the body uses energy stored in that region. This can result in loss of breast firmness."},{"x":"Aging: With increasing age, skin and muscle tone diminish, causing the breasts to sag."},{"x":"Previous Breast Augmentation: Extremely large breast augmentation can lead to a disproportionate appearance. Over time, the breasts might sag due to the excessive weight."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Methods to Solve Sagging Chest Problems with Lifting Techniques:"},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Crescent Lift Technique: Suitable for those with moderately sagging breasts. The surgeon trims the skin around the areola in a circular shape and sews it closer to the nipple."},{"x":"Mini Moon Crescent Lift: Designed for slightly sagging breasts. This technique involves lifting and reshaping the nipple and breast tissue in a crescent shape, achieving a lift of about 1-2 cm."},{"x":"Vertical Lift Technique: Applicable to significantly sagging breasts. The surgeon removes excess skin below and around the breasts, creating vertical and horizontal incisions. This method reduces breast size while providing an uplift."},{"x":"Full Vertical Lift: Similar to the vertical lift but for more pronounced sagging. This method involves exterior and interior skin removal, centralizing the nipple, and lifting the breast tissue for a prominent appearance."}]},{"t":"p","x":"For those seeking information on the best lifting techniques, Apex Medical Center is highly recommended. Apex excels in beauty enhancement, offering cutting-edge technology and modern medical instruments. The operating rooms adhere to stringent safety standards comparable to those of major hospitals. Therefore, entrusting Apex for chest enhancement ensures safety throughout the process."}],"desc":"Lift and firm your chest with Apex's top techniques. Discover effective solutions for sagging issues and regain your confidence with expert care."},"knowledge/two-levels-of-sagging-breasts-and-how-to-firm-them":{"key":"knowledge/two-levels-of-sagging-breasts-and-how-to-firm-them","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Two Levels of Sagging Breasts and How to Firm Them","excerpt":"Sagging breasts are considered a significant concern for women, as they directly impact self-confidence. But how can you determine the degree of breast sagging and take steps to address it?","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/two-levels-of-sagging-breasts-and-how-to-firm-them.webp","alt":"Two Levels of Sagging Breasts and How to Firm Them","h1":"Two Levels of Sagging Breasts and How to Firm Them","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/two-levels-of-sagging-breasts-and-how-to-firm-them.webp","alt":"Two Levels of Sagging Breasts and How to Firm Them"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Sagging breasts are considered a significant concern for women, as they directly impact self-confidence. But how can you determine the degree of breast sagging and take steps to address it? Here’s a basic self-assessment method called the Pencil Test:"},{"t":"h2","x":"Pencil Test Procedure:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Lift your breasts."},{"x":"Place a pencil under your breast’s base."},{"x":"Release your breast."},{"x":"If the pencil doesn’t fall after releasing, your breasts are starting to sag."},{"x":"If the pencil falls, your breasts are still firm."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Breast sagging levels and appropriate tightening measures:"},{"t":"p","x":"Level 1 Sagging: Breast’s nipple sags to the same level as the base of the breast."},{"t":"p","x":"Level 2 Sagging: Breast’s nipple sags below the base of the breast but remains higher than the breast crease."},{"t":"p","x":"Level 3 Sagging: Breast’s nipple sags below the breast base and points downward towards the bottom of the breast."},{"t":"p","x":"Level 4 Sagging: Breast’s areola sags significantly, potentially extending to the waistline, with the nipple pointing distinctly downward."},{"t":"h2","x":"Addressing breast sagging is personalized and depends on the degree of sagging:"},{"t":"p","x":"For Individuals with Normal Breast Base Position: If your breast base is in a normal position, addressing sagging can involve silicone augmentation to enhance the natural shape."},{"t":"p","x":"For Level 1-2 Sagging: This situation involves a moderate level of sagging. Solutions could range from silicone augmentation to surgical lifting, depending on breast tissue quality and skin condition. The surgeon will evaluate and decide whether augmentation or lifting is suitable."},{"t":"p","x":"For Level 3-4 Sagging: Significant sagging typically requires a surgical breast lift procedure. For those with Level 3-4 sagging, the technique could involve a vertical lift, which tightens excess skin and raises the nipple. In more extreme cases, a vertical lift with augmentation may be needed."},{"t":"h2","x":"Several surgical techniques for breast lift include:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Donut Mastopexy: Suitable for moderate sagging."},{"x":"Crescent Mastopexy: Ideal for mild sagging."},{"x":"Vertical Mastopexy: Suitable for moderate to severe sagging."},{"x":"Inverted T Mastopexy: Used for substantial sagging."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Choosing Apex for Safe Breast Lift:"},{"t":"p","x":"Apex is a comprehensive beauty center overseen by experienced surgeons and equipped with modern tools. Surgical rooms adhere to strict safety standards. The operating room maintains temperatures between 17-24 degrees Celsius, a humidity-controlled environment, and filtered air circulation. Adequate ventilation and temperature control ensure a comfortable experience for patients while minimizing the risk of complications."},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, determining the appropriate treatment for sagging breasts depends on the degree of sagging and individual characteristics. Consulting with experts at Apex can guide you toward the right solution, ensuring safety and satisfying results."}],"desc":"Assess breast sagging levels with Apex's guide. Discover effective solutions for firming and lifting at any stage for renewed confidence and shape."},"knowledge/how-to-maintain-beautiful-breasts":{"key":"knowledge/how-to-maintain-beautiful-breasts","cat":"Knowledge","title":"How to Maintain Beautiful Breasts","excerpt":"Breast augmentation is a common procedure in today’s era as it enhances the external appearance of women like us, making us look more confident and attractive.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/how-to-maintain-beautiful-breasts.webp","alt":"How to Maintain Beautiful Breasts","h1":"How to Maintain Beautiful Breasts","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/how-to-maintain-beautiful-breasts.webp","alt":"How to Maintain Beautiful Breasts"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation is a common procedure in today’s era as it enhances the external appearance of women like us, making us look more confident and attractive. Furthermore, breast augmentation can address the issue of sagging breasts. However, it’s important to know that the journey doesn’t end after getting breast implants. To ensure that your breasts remain beautiful over time, you need to take care of yourself."},{"t":"h2","x":"Postoperative Care After Breast Augmentation for Long-lasting Beauty"},{"t":"p","x":"During the first few weeks after breast augmentation, it’s crucial to follow the surgeon’s recommendations diligently. This includes taking the prescribed medications and avoiding over-the-counter medications, as they can lead to unexpected bleeding. You should also abstain from alcohol and smoking to prevent complications such as excessive bleeding and wound healing issues. For the first month after breast augmentation, special bras designed for post-augmentation patients, without any underwire, are recommended. This helps prevent pressure on the breasts and minimizes movement during the initial recovery period."},{"t":"h2","x":"Safe Breast Augmentation: Choose a Specialist Surgeon"},{"t":"p","x":"At Apex Medical Center, we have a specialized team of surgeons dedicated to breast augmentation procedures. Breast augmentation is a major surgical procedure that requires careful analysis and individualized planning to achieve a natural look that complements your overall body proportions. This involves choosing the right implant size that suits your body, as well as the precise technique for implant placement."},{"t":"p","x":"For instance, there are two common implant placement options: under the muscle (submuscular) and above the muscle (subglandular). Submuscular placement is suitable for those with limited natural breast tissue, as the implant is positioned beneath the chest muscle to provide adequate coverage and a more natural appearance. On the other hand, subglandular placement is suitable for those with some existing breast tissue, as the implant is positioned above the muscle."},{"t":"h2","x":"Achieving Beautifully Proportioned Breasts: Size Matters"},{"t":"p","x":"Some may think that going bigger is always better when it comes to breast augmentation. However, the trends in breast augmentation have evolved in 2023 towards achieving proportionate breast enhancement. The goal is to have breasts that are natural-looking and well-proportioned to your body. The advantages of choosing a size that fits your body’s proportions are numerous: it helps create a more natural appearance, reduces the risk of rippling around the implant, minimizes sagging, and lowers the chances of developing stretch marks."},{"t":"h2","x":"Preoperative Considerations Before Breast Augmentation"},{"t":"p","x":"Before undergoing breast augmentation surgery, there are several essential steps to take:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Fasting: Refrain from eating and drinking any liquids for at least 8 hours before the surgery to prevent potential complications related to anesthesia."},{"x":"Smoking cessation: Quit smoking for at least 2 weeks before the surgery, as nicotine can affect blood flow and healing, increasing the risk of complications."},{"x":"Alcohol avoidance: Avoid alcohol for at least 2 weeks before surgery to prevent increased bleeding during the procedure."},{"x":"Discontinuation of certain medications: If you are taking specific medications or supplements like aspirin or blood thinners, consult with your surgeon about discontinuing them in advance."},{"x":"Cleanliness: Ensure your body is thoroughly clean to reduce the risk of infection post-surgery."},{"x":"Allergies and medical history: Inform your surgeon about any allergies or previous reactions to medications."},{"x":"Nails: If you have long nails, clean them meticulously as the surgeon will measure oxygen levels from your fingertips to monitor your condition during surgery."},{"x":"Support: Bring a trusted person with you on the day of surgery for safety and assistance during the recovery process."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Postoperative Guidelines After Breast Augmentation"},{"t":"p","x":"After undergoing breast augmentation surgery, it’s essential to follow these postoperative guidelines:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Take prescribed medications as directed by your surgeon to reduce the risk of complications and promote faster wound healing."},{"x":"Refrain from smoking and alcohol consumption for at least 1-2 months to prevent breast inflammation and infections."},{"x":"Avoid strenuous physical activities and exercise that may impact your breasts for at least 2 months or until your breasts have fully healed."},{"x":"Choose soft and easily digestible foods, such as porridge or clear soups, and avoid spicy or strongly flavored foods."},{"x":"Attend all follow-up appointments with your surgeon for a thorough evaluation of your postoperative progress. These appointments are crucial for your personal well-being, as any issues can be addressed promptly by the medical team. They also ensure the best possible results and safety throughout your recovery."}]},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, if you’re considering breast augmentation, prioritizing safety and trust in the chosen medical center is paramount. Researching and gathering comprehensive information is essential, and Apex Medical Center is an excellent option for those seeking breast augmentation procedures. We have a dedicated team of surgeons who provide direct and specialized care. Additionally, we prioritize patient safety throughout the surgical process, including continuous monitoring by qualified medical professionals. Your well-being is our primary concern, and we take every precaution to ensure your safety during surgery and recovery."}],"desc":"During the first few weeks after breast augmentation, it's crucial to follow the surgeon's recommendations diligently."},"knowledge/how-safe-is-cosmetic-surgery-in-thailand":{"key":"knowledge/how-safe-is-cosmetic-surgery-in-thailand","cat":"Knowledge","title":"How Safe Is Cosmetic Surgery in Thailand","excerpt":"Over the past 10 years cosmetic surgery in Thailand has gained significant global recognition and is now one of the leading destinations for medical tourists looking for a range of treatments.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/how-safe-is-cosmetic-surgery-in-thailand.webp","alt":"How Safe Is Cosmetic Surgery in Thailand","h1":"How Safe Is Cosmetic Surgery in Thailand","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/how-safe-is-cosmetic-surgery-in-thailand.webp","alt":"How Safe Is Cosmetic Surgery in Thailand"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Over the past 10 years cosmetic surgery in Thailand has gained significant global recognition and is now one of the leading destinations for medical tourists looking for a range of treatments. But how safe is cosmetic surgery in Thailand? The short answer is that it’s very safe. As you would do in your home country, make sure you choose a clinic and surgeon who has good experience and has earned a reputation for high-quality cosmetic surgery."},{"t":"h2","x":"Medical Tourism in Thailand"},{"t":"p","x":"The medical tourism industry post-pandemic is booming, attracting millions of international patients every year. Many medical tourists choose Thailand attracted by the mix of skilled surgeons, modern medical facilities and the more affordable pricing. In 2023 the International Society of Aesthetic Plastic Surgery (ISAPS) revealed that Thailand ranks in the top 10 counties in the world for cosmetic procedures performed globally."},{"t":"p","x":"One of the main reasons for Thailand’s success in this field is the high level of training and certification among its surgeons. A lot of the surgeons in Thailand have been educated, completed training and taken part in fellowships at prestigious institutions internationally, in places like the US, UK and Australia. To add to that, hospitals and clinics in Thailand are also accredited by international organizations including the Joint Commission International (JCI) which guarantees adherence to their global safety and quality standards."},{"t":"h2","x":"Surgeons & Facilities"},{"t":"p","x":"To get the best results you’ll want to pick a surgeon with good experience and a long list of satisfied customers, along with a facility that is top of the line in terms of comfort, hygiene and use of the latest technology. You will be able to find many reputable medical centers in Thailand that maintain and exceed international standards of care and safety. More than 60% of private hospitals in Thailand are accredited by international bodies like the JCI as previously mentioned, which shows their commitment to high standards in patient and surgical outcomes."},{"t":"p","x":"You’ll also find that most Thai surgeons are board-certified and are members of international professional organizations such as the ISAPS. This level of qualification and oversight is vital for a clinic to maintain patient safety and the effectiveness of cosmetic procedures."},{"t":"h2","x":"Pricing"},{"t":"p","x":"It goes without saying that one of the main attractions of cosmetic surgery in Thailand apart from being able to combine it with a recovery holiday is the price factor. For example, breast surgery in Thailand can cost anywhere between $2000 and $6000, compared to the US where the same procedure can easily cost upwards of $10,000. The lower prices offered in Thailand are not reflective of safety or quality but are instead due to far lower operational costs in Thailand. For example, you will have the same range of implants to choose from as you would do if you were having the surgery carried out in America."},{"t":"h2","x":"Safety"},{"t":"p","x":"Cosmetic surgery is as safe as having surgery anywhere else, and that means you need to understand that with all surgery comes inherent risks. Some of the common risks that are associated with cosmetic procedures include:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Infection,"},{"x":"Scarring"},{"x":"Anesthesia complications"},{"x":"Unsatisfactory results"}]},{"t":"p","x":"To avoid this, make sure you undergo a thorough consultation, where your medical history and expectations are clearly and openly discussed with the surgeon. Choosing an accredited clinic in Thailand with highly qualified and experienced surgeons will also reduce your risks of complications during surgery."},{"t":"p","x":"To sum up and answer in short, Thailand is just as safe an option as having surgery in your home country, provided that you choose a reputable clinic. Thailand itself has stringent medical standards, internationally accredited hospitals and world-class surgeons, so patients can expect a high level of care and outcomes. Make sure you keep in mind the risks associated with your procedure and are well-informed about expectations."},{"t":"h2","x":"Thinking About Cosmetic Surgery in Thailand?"},{"t":"p","x":"At Apex Medical Center our board-certified surgeons specialize in performing a range of cosmetic procedures to the highest standards of safety and care. Get in touch today to schedule a consultation with us and take the first steps in booking your cosmetic surgery."}],"desc":"Explore the safety of cosmetic surgery in Thailand, with insights on Apex Medical Center’s trusted, professional practices."},"knowledge/essential-tips-for-breast-augmentation-recovery":{"key":"knowledge/essential-tips-for-breast-augmentation-recovery","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Essential Tips for Breast Augmentation Recovery","excerpt":"Choosing whether or not to get breast augmentation surgery is a big personal decision which can mark a transformation towards your new look.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/essential-tips-for-breast-augmentation-recovery.webp","alt":"Essential Tips for Breast Augmentation Recovery","h1":"Essential Tips for Breast Augmentation Recovery","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/essential-tips-for-breast-augmentation-recovery.webp","alt":"Essential Tips for Breast Augmentation Recovery"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Choosing whether or not to get breast augmentation surgery is a big personal decision which can mark a transformation towards your new look. However, just because you have already had the surgery, doesn’t mean you’re good to go just yet. Post-operative care is just as important to ensure you achieve the best possible results. Check out our 6 essential tips, backed up by research and studies to guide you through a successful recovery."},{"t":"h2","x":"Follow Your Surgeons Instructions"},{"t":"p","x":"First and foremost, you need to follow your surgeon’s advice. Everyone’s recovery is slightly different so tailored instructions are often provided to address your specific recovery. A study that was published in the Journal of Plastic, Reconstructive & Aesthetic Surgery highlighted the fact that patients who follow medical advice tend to experience fewer complications post-surgery along with better satisfaction levels."},{"t":"h2","x":"Wear Support Bras"},{"t":"p","x":"Supported by almost all research, the use of recommended support bras post-surgery significantly reduces swelling and helps to maintain the position of the implant. You must wear these as prescribed so they can do their job and positively influence the healing process."},{"t":"h2","x":"Rest"},{"t":"p","x":"Getting the proper amount of rest is key to recovery. This is backed up by many surgeons who emphasize the importance of avoiding strenuous activity in the period after surgery. They recommend that instead of going straight back to your normal routine, you build back to it gradually, starting with light exercise, which can promote better circulation and reduce the risk of complications like blood clots."},{"t":"h2","x":"Diet and Hydration"},{"t":"p","x":"Nutrition is extremely important to recovery and studies like the one published in the British Journal of Nursing show that a diet that is high in protein, vitamins and minerals can accelerate the body’s tissue repair abilities. As well as nutrition, keeping well hydrated is equally important as it helps with skin elasticity and your overall recovery."},{"t":"h2","x":"Keep Incision Areas Clean and Moisturized"},{"t":"p","x":"To prevent infections, you must keep the incision areas clean. At the hospital, nurses will tend to your dressings regularly and then the doctor will give you advice for home care and you must follow it. There are also a variety of topical treatments that can improve scar healing that you may be given depending on your individual circumstances."},{"t":"h2","x":"Avoid Smoking and Alcohol"},{"t":"p","x":"As you would expect, smoking is highly discouraged during your breast augmentation recovery stage. Smoking can restrict blood flow and lead to complications such as delayed wound healing and increased risk of infection. There is one study that was published in the Annals of Plastic Surgery that found that giving up smoking before surgery and refraining from smoking post-surgery dramatically improves your healing outcome. To add to that, alcohol can be just as bad as it tends to interfere with medication and aggravate swelling and bruising. Some of the best advice would be to refrain from smoking and drinking both before and after surgery until you are fully healed."},{"t":"h2","x":"Consult with Our Experts"},{"t":"p","x":"We are proud the be at the forefront of cosmetic surgery innovations in Thailand where our team of highly acclaimed specialists are dedicated to guiding you through every phase of your personalized recovery. If you are interested in breast augmentation surgery in Bangkok and would like a consultation call with our experts at Apex Medical Center, please Reach Out To Us Here."}],"desc":"Learn why Thailand is a popular destination for safe and high-quality cosmetic procedures. Get in touch with us today, call +66 85 000 2001"},"knowledge/why-is-plastic-surgery-booming-in-thailand":{"key":"knowledge/why-is-plastic-surgery-booming-in-thailand","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Why is Plastic Surgery Booming in Thailand?","excerpt":"Over the last decade, Thailand has established itself as a leading hub for cosmetic surgery, evident in its booming plastic surgery market.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Plastic-Surgery-en.webp","alt":"Why is Plastic Surgery Booming in Thailand?","h1":"Why is Plastic Surgery Booming in Thailand?","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Plastic-Surgery-en.webp","alt":"Why is Plastic Surgery Booming in Thailand?"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Over the last decade, Thailand has established itself as a leading hub for cosmetic surgery, evident in its booming plastic surgery market."},{"t":"p","x":"The current surge is driven by a combination of affordability, high-quality care and the appealing potential of combining cosmetic procedures with a tropical vacation. Let’s jump in and take a detailed look at the factors that have contributed to Thailand fast becoming the go to destination for plastic surgery."},{"t":"h2","x":"Affordability"},{"t":"p","x":"One of the main reasons people flock to Thailand for plastic surgery is the price advantage that Thailand offers. Procedures in Thailand are typically 60-70% cheaper than in Western countries. This significant price difference can be attributed to lower operational costs and strong government support for the medical tourism industry”. Despite the affordability, the quality of care remains high and in most cases, exceeds what you would get back home, making it an attractive option."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/high-quality-care-en.webp","alt":"High-Quality Care"},{"t":"h2","x":"High-Quality Care"},{"t":"p","x":"Thailand is renowned for its world-class medical facilities. Walk into any clinic or hospital and you will see why. The Hospitals and clinics , here are equipped with the latest state-of-the-art technology and staffed by highly skilled surgeons. Many of these professionals have received training and experience in Western countries, ensuring they are well-versed in the latest surgical techniques and standards. The quality of care is often compared to that of luxury hotels, providing patients with a comfortable and reassuring environment for their procedures and recovery."},{"t":"h2","x":"Medical Tourism"},{"t":"p","x":"The medical tourism market in Thailand is nothing short of thriving, attracting millions of visitors each year who are looking for medical procedures. Thailand’s strategic location, well-connected international airports, and visa-on-arrival policies for many nationalities make it an accessible destination for international patients. The ease of getting to Thailand along with the well-priced medical tourism packages provides a lot of appeal for people who are looking to combine cosmetic procedures with leisure."},{"t":"h2","x":"Latest Procedures"},{"t":"p","x":"Significant investment in the medical industry has positioned Thailand at the forefront of advanced plastic surgery techniques. Clinics and hospitals offer both invasive and non-invasive procedures, which use cutting edge technology such as AI for treatment planning and consultations. This means that outcomes have been improved and along with increased demand for innovative and less invasive cosmetic solutions."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Cultural-Acceptance-en.webp","alt":"Cultural Acceptance"},{"t":"h2","x":"Cultural Acceptance"},{"t":"p","x":"Unlike in some parts of the world, cosmetic surgery is met with a positive attitude in Thailand. Cultural acceptance creates a supportive environment where you can feel comfortable undergoing procedures. There is no negative judgment. This openness is part of the reason why many people choose Thailand as their main destination for cosmetic enhancements."},{"t":"h2","x":"Tourism Appeal"},{"t":"p","x":"Looking beyond just the operating room, Thailand offers a rich culture and fantastic tropical environment in which to recover. You can find wellness retreats everywhere in Thailand and the famed hospitality provides the perfect place to recover from your procedures. Whether this means you get to enjoy a beautiful tropical beach or a wellness retreat surrounded by nature, the opportunity to combine surgery with a holiday adds to the overall charm of choosing Thailand for plastic surgery."},{"t":"p","x":"Ready to take the next step? Contact Apex Medical Center today to learn more about how we can assist you on your cosmetic journey. Our team is here to provide expert advice and personalized consultation for your needs."}],"desc":"Over the last decade, Thailand has established itself as a leading hub for cosmetic surgery, evident in its booming plastic surgery market."},"knowledge/essential-insights-for-post-liposuction-recovery":{"key":"knowledge/essential-insights-for-post-liposuction-recovery","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Essential Insights for Post-Liposuction Recovery","excerpt":"Liposuction surgery is one of the most popular cosmetic procedures worldwide, with thousands undergoing the procedure annually to achieve a more contoured look.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Essential-Insights-for-Post-Liposuction-Recovery-en.webp","alt":"Essential Insights for Post-Liposuction Recovery","h1":"Essential Insights for Post-Liposuction Recovery","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Essential-Insights-for-Post-Liposuction-Recovery-en.webp","alt":"Essential Insights for Post-Liposuction Recovery"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Liposuction surgery is one of the most popular cosmetic procedures worldwide, with thousands undergoing the procedure annually to achieve a more contoured look. However, undergoing the surgery alone is not enough; effective recovery is essential to maximize the benefits and minimize potential complications. This guide offers evidence-based insights into the recovery process for liposuction, supported by data and expert recommendations."},{"t":"h2","x":"Recovery Phases"},{"t":"p","x":"Liposuction recovery can be divided into short and long-term phases. According to a study published by the American Society of Plastic Surgeons, immediate recovery will typically require around 5 to 7 days of rest, after which the patients can gradually return to light work and activities. Roughly 80% of patients report significant reductions in swelling within the first 4 to 6 weeks, though complete recovery can take up to 3 months as residual swelling fully subsides."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Key-Practices-for-Optimal-Recovery-en.webp","alt":"Key Practices for Optimal Recovery"},{"t":"h2","x":"Key Practices for Optimal Recovery"},{"t":"h3","x":"Compression Garments"},{"t":"p","x":"Research consistently demonstrates that wearing compression garments is highly effective in reducing postoperative edema and improving comfort. A study in the Journal of Plastic, Reconstructive & Aesthetic Surgery found that patients using compression garments experienced a 30% faster reduction in swelling compared to those who did not. These garments should be worn continuously for at least 4 to 6 weeks."},{"t":"h3","x":"Activity and Exercise"},{"t":"p","x":"Light activity is very much encouraged early on to increase circulation and reduce the risk of thrombosis. The data suggests that starting with light walking can decrease recovery time and improve overall outcomes. However, more intense physical activities should be avoided for a minimum of 4 to 6 weeks, as recommended by post-surgical care guidelines."},{"t":"h3","x":"Nutrition and Hydration"},{"t":"p","x":"Proper nutrition is always recommended and this is especially true during recovery periods. Consuming a well-balanced diet rich in protein and vitamins supports the healing process. Clinical evidence shows that adequate hydration, through water and electrolyte-rich fluids, assist in maintaining all metabolic functions and preventing constipation, a common issue post-surgery due to opioid pain management."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/How-to-Avoid-Potential-Complications-en.webp","alt":"How to Avoid Potential Complications"},{"t":"h2","x":"How to Avoid Potential Complications"},{"t":"p","x":"Liposuction is a very popular procedure that is carried out almost daily in the clinic and while it’s a very safe procedure, complications, although rare, can occur. Studies report that 5-10% of patients can expect to experience minor complications such as severe bruising or skin irregularities."},{"t":"p","x":"More severe complications like infection are rare and occur in fewer than % of cases, which is largely due to advances in surgical techniques and updated post-op care guidelines. If you have any skin issues, should be reported these to the surgeon during your initial consultation as they may increase the risk of significant side effects, such as contour irregularities."},{"t":"p","x":"The best way to avoid potential complication is discuss everything with your surgeon before surgery follow their medical advice, and maintain a healthy lifestyle during recovery."},{"t":"h2","x":"Follow-Up and Medical Guidance"},{"t":"p","x":"To make sure your recovery is on track and you are healing well during the recovery process it’s very important that you attend your follow-ups. Your follow-up appointments can allow for timely intervention if there are any complications."},{"t":"p","x":"During these meetings you can report any unexpected symptoms to your doctor, such as excessive pain or swelling. Your doctor can then either act on this and provide you with additional recovery measures or provide you with peace of mind that this is a normal part of the recovery process."},{"t":"p","x":"Proactive postoperative care has been shown to reduce recovery-related complications, such as swelling and discomfort, by up to 20%, according to recent healthcare studies"},{"t":"h2","x":"Are you thinking about getting liposuction?"},{"t":"p","x":"Contact our clinic today for a personalized consultation and discover how we can support you through every step of the procedure and recovery. The Apex team is here to answer your questions."},{"t":"p","x":"Reach out now to schedule your appointment."}],"desc":"Liposuction surgery is one of the most popular cosmetic procedures worldwide, with thousands undergoing the procedure annually to achieve a more contoured look."},"knowledge/understanding-the-recovery-timeline-for-a-breast-lift":{"key":"knowledge/understanding-the-recovery-timeline-for-a-breast-lift","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Understanding the Recovery Timeline for a Breast Lift","excerpt":"As a surgeon, one of the most common questions I get asked by patients thinking about a breast lift is the recovery timeline.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/understanding-the-recovery-timeline-for-a-breast-lift.webp","alt":"Understanding the Recovery Timeline for a Breast Lift","h1":"Understanding the Recovery Timeline for a Breast Lift","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/understanding-the-recovery-timeline-for-a-breast-lift.webp","alt":"Understanding the Recovery Timeline for a Breast Lift"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"As a surgeon, one of the most common questions I get asked by patients thinking about a breast lift is the recovery timeline. Understanding hat you can expect during the healing process can really help you prepare both, mentally and physically for your experience. I’ll walk you through the main stages of recovery to expect after a breast lift and provide some tips to improve healing."},{"t":"h2","x":"Immediate Post Operative Period"},{"t":"p","x":"Straight after surgery you’ll need to spend some time in the recovery room where our staff will monitor you as the effects of the anesthesia wear off. At this stage you need to rest and allow your body to begin the healing process. Most patients can be discharged the same day, but you’ll have to have someone to drive you and help you back to your home or hotel."},{"t":"h3","x":"The First Few Days"},{"t":"p","x":"The first few day’s post-surgery are always the most challenging as you will probably experience some swelling, bruising and moderate pain. Your surgeon will prescribe pain medication so this can be controlled and you experience minimal discomfort. You must make sure you avoid any strenuous activities and keep your upper body movements minimal. Rest is your best friend at this stage and you must give your body time to heal."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/First-Week-to-Two-Weeks.webp","alt":"First Week to Two Weeks"},{"t":"h3","x":"First Week to Two Weeks"},{"t":"p","x":"As you enter the first week to two weeks after surgery, you might notice that swelling and bruising peak before they start to subside. During this time, you can switch from prescription pain medication to over-the-counter options, as guided by your surgeon. Wearing compression garments or surgical bras as instructed is vital to support the healing process and reduce swelling."},{"t":"h3","x":"Two Weeks to One Month"},{"t":"p","x":"At the end of week 2 most patients will find they feel a lot more comfortable and notice improvements in the appearance of their breasts. The swelling and bruising at this point should continue to decrease and you can gradually resume some light activities. However, it’s still very important that you avoid anything that could potentially strain the area around your breasts. You will be provided very specific guidance on when you can return to work and other daily tasks based on your recovey."},{"t":"h3","x":"One Month and Beyond"},{"t":"p","x":"After a month, you’ll notice significant improvements in mobility and comfort. While you’ll still have some swelling, your breasts will start settling into their new position and scars will gradually fade. At this stage, you can usually get back to most normal activities, including exercise, although it’s imperative to follow your surgeon’s advice on the timing and intensity."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Long-Term-Recovery.webp","alt":"Long-Term Recovery"},{"t":"h2","x":"Long-Term Recovery"},{"t":"p","x":"The full effects of a breast lift can take several months to manifest. While your swelling and bruising can heal within weeks, attending follow-up appointments with your surgeon is crucial for monitoring the healing process. One of the main parts of healing is making sure you maintain a healthy lifestyle, which includes proper nutrition and skincare. This will help support your recovery and ensure the best chance of being fully satisfied with the results of the breast lift."},{"t":"h3","x":"Factors Influencing Recovery Time"},{"t":"p","x":"Recovery is very personalized and can vary from person to person due to several factors like your overall health, how complex the procedure was and adherence to post-op instructions. If you follow your surgeon’s guidelines to a tee can really influence your recovery experience and the final outcome of your breast lift."},{"t":"h4","x":"Tips for Managing Discomfort & Ensuring Optimal Healing"},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Pain Management: Take prescribed medication as directed and use ice packs to reduce swelling and discomfort."},{"x":"Follow-Up Appointments: These are essential for ensuring proper healing and addressing any concerns."},{"x":"Nutrition and Hydration: A balanced diet rich in protein and vitamins supports tissue repair."},{"x":"Rest and Relaxation: Listen to your body and prioritize rest to facilitate healing."},{"x":"Avoid Smoking and Alcohol: Both can hinder your body’s ability to heal and should be avoided during recovery."}]}],"desc":"As a surgeon, one of the most common questions I get asked by patients thinking about a breast lift is the recovery timeline."},"knowledge/can-breast-augmentation-be-combined-with-mammogram":{"key":"knowledge/can-breast-augmentation-be-combined-with-mammogram","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Can Breast Augmentation Be Combined with Mammogram","excerpt":"Many women consider breast augmentation for various reasons, and it’s a surgical procedure that requires precision and expertise from plastic surgeons.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/can-breast-augmentation-be-combined-with-mammogram-en.webp","alt":"Can Breast Augmentation Be Combined with Mammogram","h1":"Can Breast Augmentation Be Combined with Mammogram","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/can-breast-augmentation-be-combined-with-mammogram-en.webp","alt":"Can Breast Augmentation Be Combined with Mammogram"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Many women consider breast augmentation for various reasons, and it’s a surgical procedure that requires precision and expertise from plastic surgeons. Breast augmentation can enhance the size and shape of breasts to make them look more natural and proportionate. However, it’s essential to carefully consider the pros and cons before deciding to undergo breast augmentation, as there are different advantages and disadvantages to this procedure."},{"t":"p","x":"One common question many women have is whether they can still undergo mammography (mammogram) to screen for breast cancer after getting breast implants. Today, Apex Medical Center is here to provide valuable information for those considering breast augmentation and its implications on mammogram screenings."},{"t":"h2","x":"What Is a Mammogram?"},{"t":"p","x":"First and foremost, let’s clarify what a mammogram is. Mammography is an X-ray examination of the breast tissue. It is a method used to detect abnormalities using lower levels of radiation than conventional X-ray machines. Mammograms produce highly detailed images that can reveal even small calcifications or tiny masses within the breast tissue. Regular ultrasound machines cannot detect and visualize these abnormalities in the same way"},{"t":"h2","x":"Can You Have a Mammogram After Breast Augmentation?"},{"t":"p","x":"Certainly, after undergoing breast augmentation with silicone or saline implants, some women wonder if mammography to screen for breast cancer becomes more challenging or less effective compared to women without breast implants. It’s important to explain that in general, physicians perform mammography alongside ultrasound imaging. In the case of women with breast implants, specialized techniques are used to perform mammograms."},{"t":"p","x":"The process involves gently separating the breast tissue from the implant and compressing the breast tissue against the machine to obtain clear images and detect any abnormalities. Patients should not worry about damaging the implants because silicone implants, in particular, are designed to be durable and flexible. Therefore, mammograms do not pose a risk to silicone or saline breast implants."},{"t":"h2","x":"Preparation Before Breast Augmentation Surgery:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Fasting: Refrain from eating and drinking for at least 8 hours before breast augmentation surgery to prevent potential complications associated with ingesting food or liquids during the procedure, as anesthesia is required."},{"x":"Smoking Cessation: Quit smoking at least 2 weeks before breast augmentation surgery. Smoking contains nicotine, which can be absorbed through the skin and affect blood vessels, leading to increased risk of complications, swelling, and infection."},{"x":"Alcohol Avoidance: Avoid alcohol consumption for at least 2 weeks prior to surgery, similar to smoking, as alcohol can affect blood circulation and increase the risk of complications."},{"x":"Medication and Supplements: Discontinue vitamin supplements and medications like aspirin and non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) 1-2 weeks before breast augmentation, as they can increase the risk of bleeding during surgery."},{"x":"Nail Care: If you have long nails or nail extensions, clean them thoroughly before surgery, as surgeons will measure oxygen levels through your fingertips to monitor your condition during the procedure."},{"x":"Hygiene: Ensure you have a clean body to minimize the risk of post-surgery infection."},{"x":"Allergies: Inform your surgeon of any medication allergies before the procedure."},{"x":"Support Person: Arrange for a trusted support person to accompany you on the day of surgery to assist with post-surgical care and transportation."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Post-Breast Augmentation Surgery Guidelines:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Medication Compliance: Take prescribed medications as instructed by your surgeon to reduce the risk of complications and facilitate a smoother recovery process."},{"x":"Smoking and Alcohol: Continue to abstain from smoking and alcohol for at least 1-2 months after surgery to avoid inflammation and infection."},{"x":"Physical Activity: Avoid strenuous physical activities and exercises that may strain the chest area for at least 2 months after breast augmentation or until your surgeon advises otherwise."},{"x":"Dietary Considerations: Choose a soft diet, such as congee or broth, and avoid heavily seasoned or spicy foods immediately after surgery."},{"x":"Follow-Up Appointments: Attend all scheduled follow-up appointments with your surgeon to ensure a safe and successful recovery and address any concerns promptly."}]},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, if you are considering breast augmentation, prioritize safety and trust in the chosen medical center. Breast augmentation is a long-term commitment, so it’s crucial to gather detailed and comprehensive information. If you are researching where to get breast augmentation in 2023, Apex Medical Center is an excellent option. We have a team of experienced surgeons who provide direct and specialized care throughout the surgical process, ensuring the highest level of safety and excellent results. Our commitment is to your safety and well-being, starting from the thorough pre-operative assessments and throughout the entire surgery, including procedures like breast augmentation, liposuction, and facelifts."}],"desc":"Many women consider breast augmentation for various reasons, and it's a surgical procedure that requires precision and expertise from plastic surgeons."},"knowledge/who-are-the-ideal-candidates-for-liposuction":{"key":"knowledge/who-are-the-ideal-candidates-for-liposuction","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Who Are the Ideal Candidates for Liposuction?","excerpt":"Liposuction is a very popular cosmetic procedure, so popular in fact, that it was the top cosmetic surgical procedure in the world in 2022 and 2023, with over 2.2 million procedures Performed.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/who-are-the-ideal-candidates-for-liposuction-en.webp","alt":"Who Are the Ideal Candidates for Liposuction?","h1":"Who Are the Ideal Candidates for Liposuction?","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/who-are-the-ideal-candidates-for-liposuction-en.webp","alt":"Who Are the Ideal Candidates for Liposuction?"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Liposuction is a very popular cosmetic procedure, so popular in fact, that it was the top cosmetic surgical procedure in the world in 2022 and 2023, with over 2.2 million procedures Performed. Its popularity is based on the fact that it can remove stubborn fat deposits from specific areas on the body, which helps patients achieve their dream body contours. It is important to note, however, that liposuction should not be used as a weight loss solution but rather a procedure that targets fat that resists traditional methods of removal like diet and exercise. The results from liposuction can transform patient’s body shape which can really boost confidence or the right candidate. Let’s have a look at some examples of suitable candidates for liposuction."},{"t":"h2","x":"An Athletic Individual with Stubborn Fat"},{"t":"p","x":"As people who have stubborn fat will know, sometimes exercise and diet, no matter how vigorous simply isn’t enough and the stubborn fat remains. Common areas for stubborn fat to be found include:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Thighs"},{"x":"Hips"},{"x":"Arms"},{"x":"Abs"}]},{"t":"p","x":"Liposuction can help these fitness enthusiasts refine their physique by specifically targeting those trouble spots, allowing their hard-earned muscle definition to shine through."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/mothers-looking-to-tighten-up-en.webp","alt":"Post-Pregnancy Mothers"},{"t":"h2","x":"Post-Pregnancy Mothers Looking to Tighten Up"},{"t":"p","x":"Pregnancy brings many changes, including the potential for excess fat around the abdomen. For mothers who have returned to their pre-pregnancy weight yet struggle with stubborn belly fat that doesn’t respond to exercise, liposuction offers a way to regain their pre-baby body shape and feel more comfortable in their skin."},{"t":"h2","x":"Middle-Aged Professionals Coping with Age-Related Fat Accumulation"},{"t":"p","x":"As people age, metabolic changes can lead to the development of stubborn fat in areas such as the back or under the chin. Metabolic changes combined with a sedentary lifestyle sitting at a desk for large parts of the day are a perfect recipe for stubborn fat deposits. Middle-aged professionals who are otherwise healthy but notice these frustrating changes might consider liposuction to maintain a youthful appearance and enhance their professional and personal confidence."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/achievers-looking-for-the-final-touch-en.webp","alt":"Weight Loss Achievers Looking for the Final Touch"},{"t":"h2","x":"Weight Loss Achievers Looking for the Final Touch"},{"t":"p","x":"People who have successfully lost a lot of weight to get healthy and look good often find that some pockets of fat remain, particularly in the arms or sides. For these weight loss champions, liposuction can be the final step on their journey. They’ve worked hard in the gym, dieted, led a clean lifestyle and they are now looking to add the finishing touches to their transformation and complement their overall success."},{"t":"h2","x":"Those with Genetic Predispositions to Fat Storage"},{"t":"p","x":"Unfortunately, some people are just genetically predisposed to store fat in areas like the lower abdomen or inner thighs, despite being fit and healthy overall. Liposuction can help achieve these people a proportional body shape to align with their overall physical appearance and active lifestyle. They’ll also find it will greatly improve their self-confidence."},{"t":"p","x":"If you’re in a similar situation to any of the above or are curious to see if you would be a suitable candidate for liposuction get in touch with one of our experts at Apex Medical Centre where they will be able to offer you their expert guidance and answer any questions you may have."}],"desc":"Liposuction is a very popular cosmetic procedure, so popular in fact, that it was the top cosmetic surgical procedure in the world in 2022 and 2023, with over 2.2 million procedures Performed."},"knowledge/why-do-people-die-from-breast-augmentation":{"key":"knowledge/why-do-people-die-from-breast-augmentation","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Why Do People Die from Breast Augmentation","excerpt":"Breast augmentation surgery is a popular procedure for adjusting the size and shape of the breasts using silicone implants or synthetic breast tissue.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/why-do-people-die-from-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"Why Do People Die from Breast Augmentation","h1":"Why Do People Die from Breast Augmentation","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/why-do-people-die-from-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"Why Do People Die from Breast Augmentation"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation surgery is a popular procedure for adjusting the size and shape of the breasts using silicone implants or synthetic breast tissue. While breast augmentation can yield desired results, it carries various risks, including the potential for fatal outcomes. The causes of death associated with breast augmentation can be attributed to several factors, including choosing an inexperienced surgeon and undergoing the procedure in a facility lacking safety standards."},{"t":"h2","x":"The Importance of Board-Certified Surgeons"},{"t":"p","x":"One crucial aspect of ensuring the safety of breast augmentation is the presence of board-certified surgeons. This is because breast augmentation surgery involves the use of anesthesia, making it vital for patients to carefully select their medical professionals. Board-certified surgeons are essential as they play a central role in controlling and planning the use of anesthesia during the procedure. They are responsible for evaluating the patient’s health in detail, assessing the dosage of anesthesia required for effective pain control during surgery, and continuously monitoring the patient’s condition throughout the procedure, even before the patient loses consciousness."},{"t":"h2","x":"Safe Breast Augmentation Techniques"},{"t":"p","x":"In today’s medical landscape, there are several advanced techniques available for breast augmentation procedures, and Apex Medical Center is one such option for individuals seeking safe and natural-looking breast augmentation results. Apex Medical Center employs a range of cutting-edge techniques, including:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Minimally Invasive Surgery: Minimally invasive breast augmentation procedures involve using cameras and small incisions to achieve precise results. This approach allows surgeons to view internal structures clearly and in detail, reducing the risk of complications."},{"x":"Reduced Blood Loss: Minimally invasive techniques are associated with reduced blood loss during surgery, as surgeons can identify blood vessels and other structures more accurately. This lowers the risk of bleeding complications."},{"x":"Nerve Preservation: Nerves in the breast area are carefully preserved during surgery, reducing the risk of complications like nipple numbness. Smaller Incisions: Minimally invasive techniques result in smaller incisions, which means less scarring for patients."},{"x":"Faster Recovery: Due to reduced tissue trauma, patients undergoing minimally invasive breast augmentation tend to experience a faster and smoother recovery process compared to traditional open surgeries."},{"x":"Lower Risk of Capsular Contracture: Precise surgical techniques contribute to a lower risk of capsular contracture, a condition in which scar tissue forms around the implant and can cause discomfort or distortion of breast shape."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"Safe Operating Rooms at Apex Medical Center"},{"t":"p","x":"At Apex Medical Center, safety is paramount, and this is evident in our state-of-the-art operating rooms, which meet the highest standards of safety and hygiene. Our operating rooms maintain strict temperature and air quality controls, ensuring that the temperature remains within a safe range and that the air is adequately filtered. The air is circulated approximately 20-25 times per hour, and it undergoes extensive filtration, reaching up to 99.99% purity. The operating room is equipped with a high-efficiency particulate air (HEPA) filtration system that removes airborne particles and maintains a sterile environment."},{"t":"h2","x":"Controlling Temperature and Humidity"},{"t":"p","x":"Temperature control within the operating room is critical to prevent patient hypothermia, especially since patients undergoing breast augmentation may be partially exposed during the procedure. Maintaining humidity levels is equally important to prevent dryness in the surgical environment. Proper temperature and humidity control help ensure patient comfort and safety."},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, breast augmentation is a significant decision that should prioritize patient safety and natural-looking results. Apex Medical Center offers advanced surgical techniques and maintains the highest standards of safety in its operating rooms to provide patients with optimal outcomes. It’s crucial for individuals considering breast augmentation to consult with experienced, board-certified surgeons to achieve their desired results safely and naturally."}],"desc":"Breast augmentation surgery is a procedure for adjusting the size and shape of the breasts using silicone implants or synthetic breast tissue."},"promotion/coolsculpting-fat-reduction-only-8900-thb-from-12500-thb":{"key":"promotion/coolsculpting-fat-reduction-only-8900-thb-from-12500-thb","cat":"Promotion","title":"Coolsculpting fat reduction Only 8,900 THB From 12,500 THB","excerpt":"This is a novel system of liposuction that helps patients shape their bodies through the removal of fat. The coolsculpting device looks like a clamp with metal plates.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Coolsculpting-no-surgery-before-after.webp","alt":"Coolsculpting fat reduction Only 8,900 THB From 12,500 THB","h1":"Coolsculpting fat reduction Only 8,900 THB From 12,500 THB","date":"Update 19 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Coolsculpting-no-surgery-before-after.webp","alt":"Coolsculpting fat reduction Only 8,900 THB From 12,500 THB"},"blocks":[{"t":"h2","x":"What is Coolsculpting?"},{"t":"p","x":"This is a novel system of liposuction that helps patients shape their bodies through the removal of fat. The coolsculpting device looks like a clamp with metal plates.The skin in the target area is pulled between the two plates by a vacuum and then clamped shut. Once turned on, the machine pumps cold water between the plates."},{"t":"p","x":"The fat freezes, dies, and is then removed from the body naturally. CoolSculpting is the only fat-freezing procedure which is an FDA-cleared,"},{"t":"p","x":"* non-surgical fat-reduction treatment that uses controlled cooling to eliminate stubborn fat that resists all efforts through diet and exercise. The results are proven, noticeable, and lasting—so you’ll look great from every angle."},{"t":"h3","x":"The benefits of Coolsculpting"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Non-invasive"},{"x":"No pain"},{"x":"No scarring or physical wounds"},{"x":"Rapid recovery"}]},{"t":"h2","x":"WHO IS AN IDEAL CANDIDATE?"},{"t":"p","x":"CoolSculpting is ideal for people who are generally in good shape but have stubborn fat bulges which refuse to go away."},{"t":"p","x":"The Coolsculpting in Bangkok price at Apex Medical Center will appeal to people who have tried everything and are looking for a more effective solution. Coolsculpting is in no way an alternative to healthy"},{"t":"p","x":"diet or lifestyle."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/4-hot-spots-for-fat-loss-en.webp","alt":"4 hot spots for fat loss"},{"t":"h2","x":"Results with Coolsculpting"},{"t":"p","x":"A few days after the procedure, the cooled fat cells begin a process called “apoptosis”, cell death, and begin to shrink. These damaged fat cells are slowly digested over several months by our bodies and removed through the liver."},{"t":"p","x":"Coolsculpting in Bangkok at Apex Medical Center is highly effective and is producing consistent results for local areas of fat like the love-handles or ‘man-boobs’, though larger areas of fat may require more invasive treatments."},{"t":"p","x":"For those looking for coolsculpting in Bangkok, Apex Medical Center offers these services, which is the answer to safe and effective fat-reduction."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Coolsculpting-Elite-Review-01.webp","alt":"Coolsculpting Elite Review 04"},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Coolsculpting-Elite-Review-02.webp","alt":"Coolsculpting Elite Review 02"},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Coolsculpting-Elite-Review-03.webp","alt":"Coolsculpting Elite Review 03"}],"desc":"Coolsculpting at Apex Medical Center: Effective fat reduction at just 8,900 THB. Enjoy non-invasive, pain-free treatment with lasting results. Book now!"},"knowledge/round-vs-teardrop-find-the-best-breast-implant-for-your-body":{"key":"knowledge/round-vs-teardrop-find-the-best-breast-implant-for-your-body","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Round vs. Teardrop: Find the Best Breast Implant for Your Body","excerpt":"After discussing the pros and cons of different brands of silicone implants, today we will talk about two popular breast implant shapes: round and teardrop.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/breast-augmentation-silicone.webp","alt":"เลือกซิลิโคนเสริมหน้าอกอย่างไรให้ตอบโจทย์","h1":"Round vs. Teardrop: Find the Best Breast Implant for Your Body","date":"Update 13 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/breast-augmentation-silicone.webp","alt":"เลือกซิลิโคนเสริมหน้าอกอย่างไรให้ตอบโจทย์"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"After discussing the pros and cons of different brands of silicone implants, today we will talk about two popular breast implant shapes: round and teardrop. If you are researching breast augmentation options, this information is a must-read. Keep in mind that the choice between these two shapes depends on individual body characteristics. Let’s explore the benefits of these two popular breast implant shapes:"},{"t":"h2","x":"1. Round Silicone Breast Implants"},{"t":"p","x":"Round silicone breast implants resemble the shape of a salapaow (Chinese dumpling). They come in various sizes and may be either projecting or non-projecting. After augmentation with round silicone implants, the breasts appear full and firm, extending from the upper chest to the lower breast mound. Round implants are particularly suitable for individuals with broad shoulders, as they tend to create a well-proportioned appearance that complements the overall body structure better than teardrop implants."},{"t":"h2","x":"2. Teardrop Silicone Breast Implants"},{"t":"p","x":"Teardrop silicone breast implants mimic the natural shape of breasts, especially when a person is standing or sitting upright. They have a gently sloping profile and provide a more natural look compared to round implants. Teardrop implants are an excellent choice for individuals with narrow or petite frames. They help achieve a balanced and proportional appearance, enhancing the overall symmetry of the body."},{"t":"p","x":"However, it’s essential to emphasize that choosing the right breast implant shape is not solely about personal preference but also depends on factors like body size, shoulder width, and individual goals. Consulting with a board-certified plastic surgeon who specializes in breast augmentation is crucial. The surgeon will consider not only the implant shape but also the size and size of the silicone implants to ensure the most suitable outcome."},{"t":"h3","x":"Before undergoing breast augmentation surgery, it’s essential to follow some pre-operative guidelines:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Fasting: Avoid all food and beverages for at least 8 hours before surgery to prevent the risk of aspiration (food or drink entering the airway) during anesthesia."},{"x":"Smoking: Quit smoking at least two weeks before breast augmentation surgery, as smoking can affect blood circulation and increase the risk of complications."},{"x":"Alcohol: Avoid alcohol consumption for at least two weeks before surgery to minimize the risk of excessive bleeding."},{"x":"Medications: Discontinue the use of blood-thinning medications and supplements like aspirin, ibuprofen, and certain herbal supplements for 1-2 weeks before surgery."},{"x":"Nail Care: Ensure clean and well-groomed nails to facilitate oxygen saturation monitoring during surgery."},{"x":"Cleanliness: Maintain good personal hygiene to minimize the risk of post-operative infection."},{"x":"Allergies: Inform your surgeon about any allergies you may have before the surgery."}]},{"t":"h3","x":"After breast augmentation surgery, follow these post-operative instructions:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Medications: Take prescribed medications as directed to manage pain and reduce the risk of complications."},{"x":"Smoking and Alcohol: Continue to avoid smoking and alcohol consumption for at least 1-2 months after surgery."},{"x":"Physical Activity: Avoid strenuous exercise and activities that may impact the breasts for at least 2 months to ensure proper healing."},{"x":"Diet: Choose soft, non-acidic foods to minimize discomfort during recovery."},{"x":"Follow-up: Attend all scheduled follow-up appointments with your surgeon for a thorough evaluation of your progress."}]},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, if you are looking for the best breast augmentation options, consider Apex Medical Center as a top choice. Apex Medical Center offers the highest level of safety, expertise from board-certified plastic surgeons, cutting-edge technology, and efficient post-operative care, ensuring the best possible results for patients. Your safety and satisfaction are our top priorities."}],"desc":"Explore Apex's guide on round and teardrop breast implants. Discover which shape suits your body for a natural, balanced silhouette. Choose confidently!"},"knowledge/4-chronic-conditions-to-avoid-breast-augmentation":{"key":"knowledge/4-chronic-conditions-to-avoid-breast-augmentation","cat":"Knowledge","title":"4 Chronic Conditions to Avoid Breast Augmentation","excerpt":"Here are some important health-related considerations for individuals considering breast augmentation. It is essential to have thorough health check-ups when planning breast augmentation","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Who-should-avoid-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"4 โรคเรื้อรังที่ควรหลีกเลี่ยงการเสริมหน้าอก","h1":"4 Chronic Conditions to Avoid Breast Augmentation","date":"Update 13 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Who-should-avoid-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"4 โรคเรื้อรังที่ควรหลีกเลี่ยงการเสริมหน้าอก"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Here are some important health-related considerations for individuals considering breast augmentation. It is essential to have thorough health check-ups when planning breast augmentation, as it is a surgical procedure that must always prioritize safety. Here are four chronic conditions related to breast augmentation that individuals should be aware of"},{"t":"h2","x":"1. Weakened Immune System"},{"t":"p","x":"The immune system plays a crucial role in protecting the body from attacks by bacteria, viruses, and other potentially harmful organisms. If the immune system is compromised or not functioning properly, it can have several adverse effects on the body, including:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Increased Risk of Infection: A weakened immune system can make the body more susceptible to infections, such as the flu, fungal infections, and other contagious diseases."},{"x":"Chronic Diseases: Problems with the immune system can increase the risk of developing chronic diseases like diabetes, heart disease, and AIDS because the immune system plays a role in controlling factors related to these conditions."},{"x":"Disease Transmission: Infections can spread more easily when the immune system is weakened, contributing to the transmission of contagious diseases like viral or bacterial outbreaks."},{"x":"Allergic Reactions: Immune system issues can lead to abnormal bodily responses to foreign substances, potentially causing allergies to foods or environmental factors. This can make the body more prone to allergic reactions, including allergies to breast implants like silicone."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"2. Individuals Requiring Continuous Medication for Chronic Conditions"},{"t":"p","x":"People with chronic conditions that require continuous medication, such as diabetes or hypertension, should be cautious when considering breast augmentation. Some medications can interact with the surgical process and pose risks, such as:"},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Medication Side Effects: Certain medications may have side effects that can impact the surgical process. For example, anticoagulant medications can affect blood clotting and increase the risk of complications during breast augmentation surgery."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"3. Family History of Breast Cancer"},{"t":"p","x":"Having a family history of breast cancer can be a direct risk factor for breast augmentation surgery. Family history can serve as an indicator of the risk of developing breast cancer in the future. Regular health check-ups and cancer screenings, as recommended by a physician, are crucial to detect breast cancer early. Individuals with a family history of breast cancer should carefully weigh the risks before considering breast augmentation."},{"t":"h2","x":"4. Pregnancy"},{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation during pregnancy or while planning to become pregnant is generally not recommended. The body undergoes significant changes during pregnancy, including breast growth and development in preparation for breastfeeding. Breast augmentation during pregnancy can lead to complications during childbirth and breastfeeding. Therefore, individuals who are pregnant or planning to become pregnant should postpone breast augmentation until after childbirth and breastfeeding."},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, individuals considering breast augmentation should consult with a board-certified plastic surgeon who specializes in breast augmentation procedures. The surgeon will assess the individual’s overall health and provide personalized recommendations based on their specific medical history and needs. Choosing a reputable medical center with experienced surgeons and state-of-the-art technology, like Apex Medical Center, can ensure the safest and most effective breast augmentation results. It’s essential to prioritize safety and long-term health when considering any surgical procedure."}],"desc":"Here are some important health-related considerations for individuals considering breast augmentation."},"knowledge/how-does-breast-augmentation-differ-for-women-and-lgbt-individuals":{"key":"knowledge/how-does-breast-augmentation-differ-for-women-and-lgbt-individuals","cat":"Knowledge","title":"How Does Breast Augmentation Differ for Women and LGBT+ Individuals?","excerpt":"Breast augmentation for women and LGBT+ individuals can vary slightly due to differences in breast size and tissue composition.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Breast-augmentation-for-women-and-LGBTQ.webp","alt":"เสริมหน้าอกผู้หญิง VS LGBTQ","h1":"How Does Breast Augmentation Differ for Women and LGBT+ Individuals?","date":"Update 12 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Breast-augmentation-for-women-and-LGBTQ.webp","alt":"เสริมหน้าอกผู้หญิง VS LGBTQ"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation for women and LGBT+ individuals can vary slightly due to differences in breast size and tissue composition. The differences arise primarily from the fact that transgender women may have smaller breast sizes compared to cisgender women, and their breast tissue may also differ due to hormone therapy."},{"t":"p","x":"The process of breast augmentation involves assessing the individual’s existing breast size to determine the appropriate implant size for augmentation. However, transgender women may have concerns about going too large with breast implants. It’s important to note that excessively large breast implants can lead to various health issues, such as back pain, neck pain, and an increased risk of complications like implant rupture."},{"t":"p","x":"To achieve the desired breast size, a thorough evaluation and surgical planning by a qualified plastic surgeon are essential. This ensures that the augmentation is proportionate and safe for the individual. It’s crucial to strike a balance between achieving the desired size and maintaining a natural appearance."},{"t":"p","x":"Is It Worth It to Get Large-Sized Breast Implants? As mentioned earlier, the suitability of large-sized breast implants depends on an individual’s existing breast size and body proportions. Those with smaller breasts to begin with may not require significantly large implants to achieve their desired look, while individuals with larger ribcages and smaller breasts may opt for larger implants."},{"t":"p","x":"However, it’s important to consult with a plastic surgeon to determine the most suitable implant size based on your goals and body type. Going too large with breast implants can lead to unnatural-looking results, and it’s associated with potential health risks, so it’s crucial to find the right balance."},{"t":"p","x":"Breast Augmentation with Hybrid Y Line Technique vs. Traditional Silicone Implants Breast augmentation using the Hybrid Y Line technique combines silicone implants with the injection of the individual’s own fat. This approach is designed to provide more natural-looking results and reduce the risk of complications, especially for individuals with limited breast tissue."},{"t":"p","x":"The fat used in this procedure is typically harvested from areas like the abdomen, arms, or thighs through liposuction. The fat is then processed and purified before being injected into the breasts in addition to the silicone implants. This technique allows for better contouring of the breasts and can result in a more natural appearance."},{"t":"p","x":"Breast Augmentation with Fat Transfer: Is It Possible After Silicone Implants? Yes, it is possible to undergo breast augmentation with fat transfer after having silicone implants. Some individuals may choose this option if they want to adjust the size or achieve a more natural look after a previous breast augmentation with silicone implants."},{"t":"p","x":"Fat transfer involves liposuction to remove excess fat from one area of the body, which is then purified and injected into the breasts. This can help enhance the shape and appearance of the breasts while maintaining a natural feel and look. However, the amount of fat that can be transferred is typically limited, so significant size changes may not be achievable through fat transfer alone."},{"t":"h2","x":"Where Is the Fat Harvested for Breast Augmentation with Fat Transfer?"},{"t":"p","x":"The fat used for breast augmentation with fat transfer is usually harvested from areas with excess fat through liposuction. Common donor sites for fat harvesting include the abdomen, arms, and thighs. The choice of donor site depends on the individual’s specific needs and the availability of suitable fat deposits."},{"t":"h2","x":"Why Consider Hybrid Y Line Breast Augmentation for Transgender Women?"},{"t":"p","x":"For transgender women, Hybrid Y Line breast augmentation can be an attractive option for several reasons. Firstly, it helps minimize the risk of complications associated with silicone implants, such as implant rupture and capsular contracture, which can become more likely as individuals age. By combining silicone implants with fat transfer, the breasts can have a more natural appearance and feel, reducing the risk of future complications."},{"t":"p","x":"Additionally, Hybrid Y Line breast augmentation helps to enhance the natural contours of the breasts, making them look more proportionate and feminine. It can also address issues like asymmetry and provide a more harmonious overall appearance. This procedure takes into consideration the individual’s age and the long-term effects of silicone implants, making it a safer and more natural-looking option for transgender women."},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, breast augmentation techniques can vary depending on an individual’s goals, body type, and existing breast tissue. It’s essential to consult with a qualified plastic surgeon to discuss the best approach and achieve the desired results while ensuring safety and a natural appearance."},{"t":"h2","x":"Why Do Type Two Women Need to Enhance Their Breasts with the Hybrid Y Line Technique?"},{"t":"p","x":"For type two women, breast enhancement is another trick to transform into complete women, isn’t it? Whether it’s natural-born women or type two women, what you need to consider is the age of the silicone. In reality, silicone can stay with us indefinitely, but will our bodies accept that silicone? It depends on the care and the type used for breast augmentation."},{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation with the Hybrid Y Line technique helps cover the silicone-injected area with fat, making the body understand that the added silicone is part of our body. This reduces the chances of future ruptures that may occur. This is the cause of contracture with silicone and the associated problems when we age. Self-fat breast augmentation, therefore, helps reduce the risk of future problems."},{"t":"p","x":"Furthermore, nature is another factor in breast augmentation that can make it more complete. The fat injected into the breast area is placed around the edge of the silicone. In traditional augmentation, if it’s a type two woman with small breasts, it will make the breast shape more apparent than that of a natural woman. Fat injection makes the edge of the silicone and the breast mound look natural, like real breasts, turning you into a true woman."},{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation with the Hybrid technique requires selecting a good location; otherwise, it might fail. The Hybrid Y Line breast augmentation surgery is a relatively complicated surgical procedure that requires the expertise and experience of a surgeon. It involves not only implanting silicone but also the extraction and injection of fat into the breast area. Surgeons must be skilled in using fat suction tools to ensure the safety of the patient. The extracted fat must also undergo medical processing to ensure it remains viable. If dead fat is injected, it’s as if no fat was injected at all."},{"t":"p","x":"Apex Medical Center is a comprehensive beauty center that uses the Hybrid Y Line breast augmentation technique. Our surgeons are experts with experience in breast augmentation and fat removal. They can use fat suction tools effectively, ensuring the safety of the patient. The surgery is performed in a specially designed operating room with hospital-level standards. Type two women who are considering breast augmentation can be confident that this procedure is safe and will give them beautiful breasts that are perfectly suited for them.Breast augmentation for women and LGBT+ individuals can vary slightly due to differences in breast size and tissue composition."}],"desc":"Breast augmentation for women and LGBT+ individuals can vary slightly due to differences in breast size and tissue composition."},"knowledge/10-things-to-know-before-considering-breast-augmentation":{"key":"knowledge/10-things-to-know-before-considering-breast-augmentation","cat":"Knowledge","title":"10 Things to Know Before Considering Breast Augmentation","excerpt":"Another dream of many women who want beautiful breasts may involve breast augmentation surgery, which can help achieve proportional breast size and enhance confidence no matter the chosen style","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Things-should-know-before-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"บอกต่อ 10 สิ่งที่ต้องรู้ก่อนเสริมหน้าอก","h1":"10 Things to Know Before Considering Breast Augmentation","date":"Update 12 February 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Things-should-know-before-breast-augmentation.webp","alt":"บอกต่อ 10 สิ่งที่ต้องรู้ก่อนเสริมหน้าอก"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Another dream of many women who want beautiful breasts may involve breast augmentation surgery, which can help achieve proportional breast size and enhance confidence no matter the chosen style. However, how can you be sure that you are adequately prepared and safe before undergoing breast augmentation surgery? Today, we will take you through 10 important things to know if you are thinking about breast augmentation, so you can gather the necessary information and study further to achieve the best results. If you want to know what these 10 essential points are, let’s take a look together."},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Ask Yourself Why You Want Breast Augmentation Certainly, breast augmentation is not just about making your breasts larger, but it’s also about addressing issues related to the proportionality of your breasts, making them fit your body shape. Breast augmentation can also help women who have sagging breasts due to reasons like breastfeeding or significant weight loss. The advantage of breast augmentation for addressing sagging breasts is that it can provide better results after the procedure. Additionally, it can make your breasts look more attractive and harmonious with your body."},{"x":"Check Your Physical Health Before Breast Augmentation Before deciding on any surgery, the first thing to be cautious about is checking your physical health concerning the specific procedure you are considering. For breast augmentation, it’s crucial to thoroughly examine whether your breasts may have the potential for lumps or breast cancer. You can conduct preliminary self-examinations by feeling your breasts for any irregularities, or you can consult a specialized physician at a hospital for a more comprehensive examination."},{"x":"Ensure the Safety and Trustworthiness of the Silicone Implants When it comes to breast augmentation with silicone implants, whether they are textured or smooth, it is essential that they meet the standards set by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) to ensure safety for patients. For example, you may have consulted with your doctor about using a specific brand and size of silicone implants, but when it comes to the actual surgery day, your surgeon may use a different brand that you’re unaware of. This can happen due to the surgical process, and it’s crucial to verify that the silicone implants used are genuine and have been properly certified."},{"x":"Research and Understand the Differences Between Silicone Implant Brands In making your decision regarding breast augmentation, it’s essential to research and understand the differences between various silicone implant brands. You should be well-informed about the advantages and disadvantages of each brand, as well as how they may affect the feel and appearance of your breasts post-surgery. For example, two popular silicone implant brands are Mentor and Motiva, each with its own set of pros and cons."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Mentor Silicone Implants: Mentor is a highly popular silicone implant brand known for its long-standing reputation for safety and quality. It is produced in the Netherlands and has received certification from both the U.S. FDA and Thai FDA. Mentor silicone implants come in both textured and smooth options. They are known for their firm texture, which reduces rippling and provides a natural appearance. The choice between round and teardrop shapes allows for customization, ensuring a natural and soft feel."},{"t":"p","x":"Advantages: Mentor silicone implants provide firmness, reduce skin wrinkling, and offer natural results. They are suitable for those with minimal breast tissue."},{"t":"p","x":"Disadvantages: The density and weight of Mentor implants can cause discomfort for some patients, especially those with minimal breast tissue."},{"t":"p","x":"Motiva Silicone Implants: Motiva is considered one of the top premium silicone implant brands. Motiva implants are made using the innovative Progressive Gel Ultima technology, resulting in a highly cohesive and soft feel. The outer shell of Motiva implants resembles both textured and smooth surfaces, reducing the risk of rippling and minimizing the chance of capsular contracture. One unique feature of Motiva implants is the inclusion of a chip with information about the implant’s model, size, and surgical date, making it easier to track and ensure safety."},{"t":"h2","x":"Silicone Texture for Breast Augmentation"},{"t":"p","x":"Textured Silicone","b":1},{"t":"p","x":"The feel of textured silicone is not slippery when it enters the breasts. It also helps the muscles inside the breasts adhere to the silicone better, preventing it from slipping from its original shape. It is more suitable for women with less breast tissue."},{"t":"p","x":"Smooth Silicone","b":1},{"t":"p","x":"The feel of smooth silicone is smoother and softer. After it is inserted into the breasts, it quickly returns to its original shape. This makes it look natural and easy to care for. However, because it is soft and easily affected by gravity, there may be cases where it shifts easily, so it is advisable not to use too much force in the early stages to avoid shaking the breasts. You should also wear a sports bra to protect the silicone and maintain the original shape in the early stages."},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Choose the silicone size that suits your proportions Some people may think that getting breast augmentation means going big from the start to avoid regret later on. However, it’s important to note that trends in breast augmentation have changed in 2023. It’s all about achieving a natural look that complements your body proportions. The benefits of choosing the right silicone size for your proportions include giving your breasts a natural appearance, allowing you to dress in any style without looking overly provocative, reducing the risk of complications such as rippling or visible silicone waves. Additionally, it helps prevent excessive sagging of the breasts due to the weight of larger silicone implants. Therefore, opting for a size that suits your body not only eliminates worries but also ensures the most natural results."},{"x":"Select surgical techniques that result in smaller incisions In the realm of breast augmentation, modern technology and surgical techniques play a crucial role in achieving better results. Today, there is minimally invasive surgery with the use of endoscopic techniques that provide highly efficient results. Plastic surgeons have developed these techniques to clearly visualize the internal structure of the body and achieve precision up to 1,000 times greater than traditional methods. There are several advantages to using endoscopic techniques, including:"}]},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"High precision: Endoscopic surgery employs high-resolution cameras, allowing surgeons to see detailed internal structures with clarity and precision."},{"x":"Reduced blood loss: Endoscopic surgery minimizes blood loss during the procedure, as it can pinpoint the location of blood vessels and details in organs that are not visible to the naked eye. This significantly lowers the risk of hematoma formation."},{"x":"Lower risk of nipple necrosis: Endoscopic surgery reduces the risk of nipple necrosis, as it allows surgeons to precisely identify nerve locations, resulting in less damage to blood supply. This greatly improves post-operative outcomes."},{"x":"Smaller incisions: Endoscopic breast augmentation results in smaller incisions, as the camera allows for a more precise view of tissue. Consequently, incisions heal into smaller scars that are only visible in the areas where the surgery took place."},{"x":"Faster recovery: Due to minimal tissue damage, endoscopic breast augmentation generally offers a faster recovery time compared to traditional methods."}]},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Understand the importance of proper silicone placement for your breast’s position The placement of silicone implants significantly impacts the outcome of breast augmentation. There are two main placement options: submuscular (under the chest muscle) and subglandular (above the chest muscle). For instance, submuscular placement is suitable for individuals with minimal existing breast tissue. In this procedure, the surgeon places the silicone implants under the chest muscle to prevent movement and ensure a natural look. It also reduces the risk of capsular contracture (hardening of the scar tissue around the implant)."},{"x":"Choose breast augmentation by a specialized and trustworthy surgeon only The first thing to consider before undergoing surgery is that the surgeon must have approved qualifications and specialized certification in the field of plastic surgery and cosmetic enhancement from the Medical Council of Thailand and the Medical Association. This involves completing a 5-year or 7-year training program in the field of plastic surgery. Dr. Somboon Waiprib, with a comprehensive track record as mentioned earlier, has also received the prestigious Global Health Asia Pacific award three times. This assures those seeking information about breast augmentation that getting the procedure done at Apex Medical Center will undoubtedly yield safe and excellent results."},{"x":"Have a board-certified anesthesiologist oversee the entire surgery duration for maximum safety Procedures that involve long surgical durations often require the use of anesthesia, just like at Apex Medical Center, where patient safety is paramount. Therefore, the surgical duration must be supervised by a board-certified anesthesiologist throughout every step. This includes conducting thorough health checks to assess the appropriate amount of anesthesia required. Furthermore, during the surgery, the anesthesiologist will continuously monitor vital signs such as heart rate, blood pressure, and oxygen levels to ensure the patient’s safety during procedures with extended surgical durations, such as breast augmentation, liposuction, facelifts, and more."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Pre-operative and Post-operative Breast Augmentation Care Guidelines","b":1},{"t":"p","x":"Pre-operative Breast Augmentation Care Guidelines:","b":1},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Avoid all food and drinks for at least 8 hours before undergoing breast augmentation surgery to prevent potential risks related to food or liquid entering the airways due to the use of anesthesia."},{"x":"Refrain from smoking for at least 2 weeks before breast augmentation surgery, as nicotine can seep through the skin and affect blood circulation, leading to swelling and an increased risk of infection."},{"x":"Abstain from consuming alcohol for at least 2 weeks prior to surgery, as it can stimulate blood circulation throughout the body, potentially causing slower blood clotting than usual."},{"x":"Discontinue the intake of vitamin supplements and medications in the aspirin category for 1-2 weeks before undergoing breast augmentation surgery, as these can increase the risk of excessive bleeding during the procedure."},{"x":"Clean and trim your nails thoroughly before surgery, as the surgeon will measure oxygen levels from your fingertips to monitor your condition during the operation."},{"x":"Ensure your body is clean and free of any potential sources of infection before undergoing breast augmentation surgery."},{"x":"Inform the medical team of any allergies to medications prior to surgery. Arrange for a trusted companion to accompany you on the day of surgery to prevent accidents and provide post-"},{"x":"operative care."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Post-operative Breast Augmentation Care Guidelines:","b":1},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"Strictly follow the prescribed medication regimen provided by your surgeon to reduce the risk of complications and promote faster healing."},{"x":"Refrain from smoking and consuming alcohol for at least 1-2 months after surgery to prevent inflammation and infection of the breasts."},{"x":"Avoid strenuous physical activities and exercises that may impact the breasts for at least 2 months or until the breasts have fully healed."},{"x":"Opt for a soft and bland diet, such as congee or rice porridge, to ease digestion and minimize potential discomfort."},{"x":"Attend all follow-up appointments with your surgeon after breast augmentation surgery for personal benefits. If any issues arise, your surgeon can address them promptly, ensuring the best and safest results."}]},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, for those seeking information on where to get the best breast augmentation, we highly recommend Apex Medical Center as a top choice. Apex prioritizes patient safety, boasts expert surgeons, utilizes cutting-edge technology, and delivers highly effective and secure breast augmentation results for all women."}],"desc":"Another dream of many women who want beautiful breasts may involve breast augmentation surgery,"},"knowledge/3-reasons-for-stiff-breast-after-breast-augmentation":{"key":"knowledge/3-reasons-for-stiff-breast-after-breast-augmentation","cat":"Knowledge","title":"3 Reasons for Stiff Breast After Breast Augmentation","excerpt":"Breast augmentation has been done, but the breasts are stiff! Stiff breasts after breast augmentation can be a significant concern for women who have undergone breast surgery.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Why-breast-augmentation-make-hard.webp","alt":"ทำไมเสริมหน้าอกแล้วแข็ง","h1":"3 Reasons for Stiff Breast After Breast Augmentation","date":"Update 12 January 2025","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Why-breast-augmentation-make-hard.webp","alt":"ทำไมเสริมหน้าอกแล้วแข็ง"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation has been done, but the breasts are stiff! Stiff breasts after breast augmentation can be a significant concern for women who have undergone breast surgery. There can be various causes for breast stiffness, including implant encapsulation, seroma formation, or even excessive scar tissue. In this article, we will discuss the three main reasons for stiff breasts after breast augmentation. If you are looking for information and are worried about experiencing such symptoms, read on to learn more."},{"t":"h2","x":"3 Causes of Breast Stiffness"},{"t":"list","o":true,"items":[{"x":"Implant Encapsulation: One of the primary reasons for breast stiffness is implant encapsulation, which can result from Staph Species bacteria surrounding the breast implant. This leads to the body’s immune response, causing the formation of scar tissue around the implant and resulting in breast stiffness."},{"x":"Seroma Formation: Another cause is the formation of seroma, which is the accumulation of yellowish fluid around the breast implant or in the empty space between the implant and the breast tissue. This can lead to the development of scar tissue and, subsequently, breast stiffness."},{"x":"Hematoma: Some women may experience bleeding and excessive blood accumulation after breast augmentation surgery. This risk depends on various factors, including pre- and post-operative care, such as the avoidance of alcohol and smoking. Blood accumulation can lead to the development of scar tissue and breast stiffness."}]},{"t":"h2","x":"How Dangerous Is Capsular Contracture?"},{"t":"p","x":"The severity of capsular contracture depends on whether the patient follows up with their plastic surgeon for regular breast examinations. If a woman notices breast stiffness after augmentation, it is essential to consult a surgeon promptly. In some cases, massaging the breasts may help relax the implant and reduce stiffness. However, if the issue persists, surgical intervention may be necessary, either by releasing the contracture or replacing the implants."},{"t":"p","x":"What to Know for a Safe and Risk-Free Breast Augmentation","b":1},{"t":"list","o":false,"items":[{"x":"The choice of implant placement, above or below the muscle, is crucial. The risk of capsular contracture is approximately 8-12% when the implant is placed under the muscle and 12-18% when placed above the muscle."},{"x":"Post-operative breast massage is recommended to prevent capsular contracture and maintain a natural appearance."},{"x":"Before breast augmentation surgery, it’s crucial to avoid alcohol and smoking for at least one month. Both substances can affect blood flow and increase the risk of complications during surgery."},{"x":"Taking a break from vitamin supplements and herbal medications for at least two weeks to one month before and after breast augmentation is advisable to prevent bleeding issues."},{"x":"Choose an implant size that is appropriate for your body and proportions. Oversized implants can increase the risk of complications, including capsular contracture."},{"x":"Avoid excessive manipulation or squeezing of the breasts shortly after surgery, as it can contribute to hematoma formation and other complications."}]},{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation is a significant surgical procedure, and the experience of the surgeon plays a crucial role in ensuring a safe outcome. Apex Medical Center is a renowned beauty enhancement center with experienced, board-certified plastic surgeons specializing in breast augmentation. With advanced technology and state-of-the-art facilities, patient safety and satisfaction are their top priorities. Their team of expert surgeons, including Associate Professors with over 20 years of experience, ensures that patients receive the highest quality care and results."},{"t":"p","x":"We hope this information helps you make informed decisions about breast augmentation and ensures a safe and successful procedure."}],"desc":"Learn why breasts may feel stiff after augmentation and how Apex can help. Get expert advice for a smooth recovery."},"knowledge/top-5-essential-questions-answered-for-women-considering-breast-surgery":{"key":"knowledge/top-5-essential-questions-answered-for-women-considering-breast-surgery","cat":"Knowledge","title":"Top 5 Essential Questions Answered for Women Considering Breast Surgery","excerpt":"Choosing to undertake breast surgery, such as augmentation, reduction, reconstruction and lifts, is a significant decision for many women.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/women-considering-breast-surgery-en.webp","alt":"Top 5 Essential Questions Answered for Women Considering Breast Surgery","h1":"Top 5 Essential Questions Answered for Women Considering Breast Surgery","date":"Update 19 September 2024","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/women-considering-breast-surgery-en.webp","alt":"Top 5 Essential Questions Answered for Women Considering Breast Surgery"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Choosing to undertake breast surgery, such as augmentation, reduction, reconstruction and lifts, is a significant decision for many women. As medical technology advances so does the knowledge and understanding of these procedures. I’ve taken the time to look at the data and highlight some of the most commonly asked questions by women who are thinking about getting breast surgery."},{"t":"h2","x":"1) Will Breast Augmentation Increase My Risk of Breast Cancer?"},{"t":"p","x":"Breast augmentation does not increase the risk of breast cancer. According to a study in the Journal of the National Cancer Institute, there is no significant association between breast implants and an increased risk of breast cancer. That being said, implants can sometimes obscure mammogram images, so just inform your radiologist about your implants before the procedure because they will need to take 4 extra pictures (2 on each breast) to get the information they need."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Old-for-Breast-Surgery.webp","alt":"Am I Too Old for Breast Surgery?"},{"t":"h2","x":"2) Am I Too Old for Breast Surgery?"},{"t":"p","x":"Age alone is not a contraindication for breast surgery. A study published in the Aesthetic Surgery Journal found that health status, rather than age, is a more critical factor in determining surgical outcomes. A lot of women over 50 choose to undergo breast surgery and have it completed successfully. As long as they are in good health and are realistic with their expectations they can achieve excellent outcomes."},{"t":"h3","x":"3) What Are the Risks of Breast Surgery?"},{"t":"p","x":"Like any surgical procedure, breast surgery carries with it certain risks such as infection, bleeding, and scarring. The American Society of Plastic Surgeons shows that complications as a result of breast surgery are relatively rare and occur in less than 5% of cases. Long-term complications can include implant rupture and capsular contracture, both are rare, but increase the longer you keep your implants. Implants are generally good to last between 10-20 years, but there is no hard or fast rule to this, some will be able to keep theirs in longer while others will require a replacement sooner. Make sure you discuss all potential risks with your surgeon during the initial consultation."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Right-Size-for-Breast-Augmentation.webp","alt":"How Do I Choose the Right Size for Breast Augmentation?"},{"t":"p","x":"To choose a suitably sized implant you need to take into account your body type, lifestyle and aesthetic goal. A study in the Plastic and Reconstructive Surgery Journal emphasizes the importance of proportionality to achieve the best looking outcomes. Surgeons now, often use 3D imaging to help patients visualize potential results before surgery to make sure they are happy with the size. It’s advisable to test different sizes during your consultation to make a judgment on what feels most comfortable."},{"t":"h2","x":"5) Can I Breastfeed After Breast Augmentation?"},{"t":"p","x":"Many women can successfully breastfeed after breast augmentation surgery. Research published in the International Breastfeeding Journal indicates that augmentation does not significantly affect milk production if the incisions are made away from the areola. However, some women may experience reduced nipple sensation, which could impact breastfeeding. Breast surgery typically does not affect glandular tissue, so breastfeeding is unlikely to be affected unless the implant placement disrupts the milk ducts."},{"t":"p","x":"If you want to breastfeed post breast surgery, make this known during your initial consultation so that the surgeon can take this into account when providing you with surgery recommendations."},{"t":"p","x":"Are you ready to transform your confidence? Contact Apex Medical Center today to speak to one of our expert breast surgery consultations. Take the first step towards achieving your confident new look!"}],"desc":"Choosing to undertake breast surgery, such as augmentation, reduction, reconstruction and lifts, is a significant decision for many women"},"knowledge/what-is-filler-injection":{"key":"knowledge/what-is-filler-injection","cat":"Knowledge","title":"What is Filler injection?","excerpt":"Filler is a substance that is injected into the skin to add volume, fill in wrinkles, and smooth out fine lines. It is commonly used in cosmetic procedures to enhance the appearance of the face","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Filler-injectio-en.webp","alt":"Filler injection","h1":"What is Filler injection?","date":"Update 19 February 2020","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Filler-injectio-en.webp","alt":"Filler injection"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Filler is a substance that is injected into the skin to add volume, fill in wrinkles, and smooth out fine lines. It is commonly used in cosmetic procedures to enhance the appearance of the face, hands, and other areas of the body. Filler is typically made from hyaluronic acid, a substance naturally found in the body, or other materials such as calcium hydroxyapatite or poly-L-lactic acid. Different types of fillers have different consistencies and are used for different areas of the face or body. Filler injections are a non-surgical alternative to traditional facelifts and other cosmetic procedures, and are generally considered safe and effective when performed by a licensed and experienced injector."},{"t":"h2","x":"Filler injections are considered good for a number of reasons."},{"t":"p","x":"First, they are a non-surgical alternative to traditional cosmetic procedures such as facelifts, which can be expensive and require a longer recovery time. Filler injections are relatively quick and easy to perform, with most procedures taking less than an hour to complete."},{"t":"p","x":"Second, filler injections can help to enhance the appearance of the face by adding volume and smoothing out wrinkles and fine lines. They can be used to fill in hollow areas of the face, such as under the eyes or in the cheeks, and can also be used to contour and define certain areas of the face."},{"t":"p","x":"Third, filler injections are temporary and reversible. Most types of fillers will eventually be absorbed by the body, typically within 6 to 12 months, and can be easily removed if necessary."},{"t":"p","x":"Fourth, filler injections are generally considered safe when performed by a licensed and experienced injector. While there are potential risks and complications associated with any cosmetic procedure, such as bruising or swelling, serious complications are rare."},{"t":"p","x":"Overall, filler injections are a good option for individuals who are looking to enhance the appearance of their face without undergoing surgery, and who are interested in a relatively quick and easy procedure with little to no downtime."},{"t":"p","x":"The ideal candidate for filler injections is someone who is looking to enhance the appearance of their face by adding volume, filling in wrinkles or fine lines, and contouring specific areas. Filler injections are suitable for individuals who are in good health and have realistic expectations for the results of the procedure."},{"t":"h2","x":"Specifically, candidates for filler injections may have :"},{"t":"p","x":"Hollow or sunken areas of the face, such as under the eyes or in the cheeks. Fine lines or wrinkles around the mouth, nose, or forehead. Lost volume in the lips or other areas of the face. Uneven or asymmetrical features that they would like to improve. It is important to note that filler injections are not suitable for everyone. Individuals with certain medical conditions or allergies may not be good candidates for the procedure, and it is important to discuss your medical history and any concerns you may have with your healthcare provider before undergoing treatment."},{"t":"p","x":"Overall, the best way to determine if you are a good candidate for filler injections is to consult with a licensed and experienced injector who can evaluate your individual needs and recommend the best course of treatment."},{"t":"h2","x":"If you are considering getting filler injections, there are several things you can do to prepare yourself for the procedure :"},{"t":"p","x":"Do your research: Before getting filler injections, it’s important to research the procedure, the different types of fillers available, and the risks and benefits associated with the procedure. This will help you to make an informed decision about whether filler injections are right for you."},{"t":"p","x":"Choose a licensed and experienced injector: It’s important to choose a healthcare provider who is licensed and experienced in administering filler injections. Ask for recommendations from friends or family members, or research online to find a qualified injector."},{"t":"p","x":"Consult with your healthcare provider: Before getting filler injections, you should schedule a consultation with your healthcare provider to discuss your goals, any medical conditions or allergies you may have, and to ask any questions you may have about the procedure."},{"t":"p","x":"Avoid blood-thinning medications: Certain medications, such as aspirin and ibuprofen, can increase the risk of bruising and bleeding after filler injections. Be sure to avoid these medications for several days before the procedure, as directed by your healthcare provider."},{"t":"p","x":"Avoid alcohol and caffeine: Consuming alcohol or caffeine can dehydrate the skin and increase the risk of swelling after filler injections. Be sure to avoid these substances for several days before the procedure."},{"t":"p","x":"Plan for downtime: While filler injections are generally quick and easy procedures, you may experience some swelling or bruising afterward. Be sure to plan for some downtime and avoid any social or work-related obligations for a day or two after the procedure."},{"t":"p","x":"By following these tips, you can help to ensure that you are prepared for filler injections and achieve the best possible results from the procedure."},{"t":"h2","x":"Aftercare for filler injections is important to ensure that you achieve the best possible results and to minimize the risk of complications. Here are some general tips to follow after getting filler injections :"},{"t":"p","x":"Avoid touching or rubbing the treated area for at least 24 hours after the procedure. Avoid strenuous physical activity or exercise for at least 24 hours after the procedure. Avoid exposure to heat or sun for at least 24 hours after the procedure. Apply ice to the treated area to reduce swelling and bruising. Avoid drinking alcohol or taking blood thinners for at least 24 hours after the procedure. Sleep on your back with your head elevated to reduce swelling. Stay hydrated by drinking plenty of water and avoiding caffeine and alcohol. It is important to follow any specific instructions provided by your healthcare provider after getting filler injections, as they may vary depending on the type of filler used and the area treated. If you experience any unusual symptoms, such as severe pain or swelling, fever, or difficulty breathing, contact your healthcare provider immediately."}],"desc":"Restore youthful volume with Apex’s filler injections. Non-surgical treatments to rejuvenate your appearance and smooth wrinkles."},"knowledge/how-to-injection-lip-in-older-people":{"key":"knowledge/how-to-injection-lip-in-older-people","cat":"Knowledge","title":"How to Injection Lip in older people","excerpt":"Lip injections are a popular cosmetic treatment that can help enhance the appearance of lips by adding volume and shape. As people age, they may notice a loss of volume and definition in their lips","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/How-to-Injection-Lip-in-older-people-en.webp","alt":"How to Injection Lip in older people","h1":"How to Injection Lip in older people","date":"Update 19 February 2020","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/How-to-Injection-Lip-in-older-people-en.webp","alt":"How to Injection Lip in older people"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Lip injections are a popular cosmetic treatment that can help enhance the appearance of lips by adding volume and shape. As people age, they may notice a loss of volume and definition in their lips, which can be addressed with lip injections. However, it’s important to approach lip injections in older people with caution and a unique approach to ensure the best results."},{"t":"h2","x":"Here are some key factors to consider when injecting lips in older people:"},{"t":"h3","x":"Type of Filler :"},{"t":"p","x":"Choosing the right type of filler is crucial when injecting lips in older people. Hyaluronic acid (HA) fillers, such as Restylane and Juvederm, are commonly used for lip injections due to their ability to plump and hydrate the lips. HA fillers are also reversible, which can provide added peace of mind for older patients. However, it’s important to note that some fillers may be more suitable for older patients with thinner lips or fine lines around the mouth."},{"t":"h3","x":"Amount of Filler :"},{"t":"p","x":"Older patients may require less filler than younger patients to achieve the desired results. This is because older patients tend to have thinner skin and less elasticity, which means that adding too much filler can make the lips look unnatural or overly puffy. A skilled injector will be able to determine the right amount of filler based on the patient’s individual needs and goals."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/medium-shot-woman-with-hyaluronic-acid-injection-scaled-en-e1739950647670.webp","alt":"medium shot woman with hyaluronic acid injection scaled"},{"t":"h3","x":"Technique :"},{"t":"p","x":"The technique used to inject lips in older people may differ from that used in younger patients. For example, injecting the filler along the border of the lips can help create a more defined and youthful appearance. Injecting the filler into the vermillion border, or the area where the lips meet the skin, can also help to smooth out fine lines and wrinkles around the mouth."},{"t":"h3","x":"Downtime and Recovery :"},{"t":"p","x":"Older patients may require more time to recover after lip injections. It’s important to advise patients to avoid strenuous exercise, hot temperatures, and alcohol for at least 24 hours after the procedure to minimize the risk of bruising or swelling. Patients should also avoid applying any pressure to the lips and refrain from wearing lipstick or lip balm for at least 24 hours after the procedure."},{"t":"p","x":"In conclusion, injecting lips in older people requires a unique approach and careful consideration of various factors. By choosing the right type of filler, determining the appropriate amount of filler, using the right technique, and allowing for adequate recovery time, older patients can achieve natural-looking and youthful lips with lip injections. Be sure to consult with a skilled and experienced injector to determine the best approach for your individual needs and goals."}],"desc":"Learn about lip injections for older individuals. Apex offers effective treatments to restore youthful lips with expert care."},"review/breast-augmentation-journey-10-years-of-confidence":{"key":"review/breast-augmentation-journey-10-years-of-confidence","cat":"Review","title":"Breast Augmentation Journey: 10 Years of Confidence","excerpt":"Hello ladies! The remarkable story of Foxy Megus Pusita Likitrattanakul is something you won’t want to miss. She’s here to share her experience with breast augmentation.","img":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/10-years-of-confidence-en.webp","alt":"Breast Augmentation Journey: 10 Years of Confidence","h1":"Breast Augmentation Journey: 10 Years of Confidence","date":"Update 19 February 2020","hero":{"src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/10-years-of-confidence-en.webp","alt":"Breast Augmentation Journey: 10 Years of Confidence"},"blocks":[{"t":"p","x":"Hello ladies! The remarkable story of Foxy Megus Pusita Likitrattanakul is something you won’t want to miss. She’s here to share her experience with breast augmentation. If you don’t want to miss out on a Foxy journey, keep on reading. First and foremost, let me start by saying, “I’ve had breast augmentation for 10 years now.” Yes, you read that right. Over this long period, my breasts faced an issue – they became firm, almost like blocks, lacking their natural movement. Dressing up and feeling confident became a challenge due to these changes."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/breast-augmentation-journey-en-1.webp","alt":"breast augmentation journey"},{"t":"p","x":"When faced with a challenge, Foxy Megus didn’t stand still. I embarked on a quest for information on how to fix my breasts. That’s when I discovered Dr. Somboon Waiprib at Apex Medical Center. Dr. Somboon’s reputation and preliminary information assured me that he was a directly skilled surgeon. This gave me the confidence I needed, and I knew I was making the right decision by choosing Apex and Dr. Somboon Waiprib for my breast augmentation."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/breast-augmentation-journey-en-2.webp","alt":"breast augmentation journey"},{"t":"p","x":"I vividly remember the excitement as I entered Apex. The innovation and numerous accolades showcased there were truly impressive. But let’s be clear, I wasn’t just there for breast enhancement; I wanted a lot more done. Driven by enthusiasm, I explained the issue with my breasts, just as I had mentioned earlier. Dr. Somboon Waiprib identified that my breasts were firm due to excessive contracting of the pectoral muscles and that the silicone implants I had were positioned too high, causing unnatural firmness."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/breast-augmentation-journey-en-3.webp","alt":"breast augmentation journey"},{"t":"p","x":"Dr. Somboon Waiprib suggested that the appropriate silicone implants for me were the Joy By Motiva ones. These implants had a broader base than the previous Motiva version, allowing for better adjustment and a more natural distribution. He also explained that with Motiva Ergonomix implants, the breast’s natural movement is improved by up to 60%, compared to 56.4% with the Motiva Ergonomix version. This was music to my ears!"},{"t":"p","x":"I felt secure and well-cared for throughout the surgical journey, thanks to the attentive medical team at Apex."},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/breast-augmentation-journey-en-4.webp","alt":"Before the Breast Augmentation"},{"t":"p","x":"Before the Breast Augmentation","b":1},{"t":"img","src":"~/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/breast-augmentation-journey-en-5.webp","alt":"7 days after the procedure:"},{"t":"p","x":"7 days after the procedure:","b":1},{"t":"p","x":"Now, Foxy Megus has completed her breast augmentation journey, and it’s been 7 days since the procedure. There might still be some swelling, but what I can truly feel is that my breasts are no longer like blocks, and they’re not as high as they used to be. Just a light touch with my fingers reveals the newfound softness of my breasts. I can confidently say that in just 7 days, I’m already impressed. Stay tuned for more updates in 1-3 months. But for today, I’m going to relax and take a breather. Goodbye for now!"}],"desc":"Discover Foxy's 10-year breast augmentation journey with Apex. Experience enhanced confidence and natural results. Transform your look today!"}},"page":{"h1":"Blog","cats":["Review","Promotion","Knowledge"],"catH":"Category"}};
